WEBVTT

00:00:09.388 --> 00:00:36.971
King Solomon's Mines Southern Africa in the year 1870 Have you found the boy, Omboppa?

00:00:37.031 --> 00:00:38.902
Yes, Omboppa.

00:00:38.962 --> 00:00:40.102
Bring him here.

00:00:40.122 --> 00:00:41.783
Yes, Omboppa.

00:00:41.843 --> 00:00:47.236
Bring the prisoner!

00:00:47.296 --> 00:00:53.989
Are you the boy they call Omboppa?

00:00:54.049 --> 00:00:58.451
Don't dishonor me by pretending that you do not know my name.

00:00:58.511 --> 00:01:00.832
I am your chief.

00:01:00.892 --> 00:01:03.232
Call me Encholo.

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:04.653
I will not do that.

00:01:04.713 --> 00:01:06.973
Call me Encholo.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:07.803
Never.

00:01:07.863 --> 00:01:09.714
You are not my chief.

00:01:09.774 --> 00:01:12.054
I am your chief.

00:01:12.114 --> 00:01:13.954
Address me as Encholo.

00:01:14.014 --> 00:01:15.645
All you will die.

00:01:15.704 --> 00:01:17.645
You are not my chief.

00:01:17.705 --> 00:01:20.305
My father, Imotou was chief.

00:01:20.365 --> 00:01:23.956
Your father is dead.

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:25.976
So, I am chief.

00:01:26.036 --> 00:01:29.065
You are only ten years old.

00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:31.994
You are not a man.

00:01:32.054 --> 00:01:36.065
Then my uncle Quasie should rule until I am a man.

00:01:36.125 --> 00:01:37.836
Quasie?

00:01:37.896 --> 00:01:40.146
Yes, Encolo, Chief Gagul.

00:01:40.206 --> 00:01:43.418
You are this boy's uncle.

00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:47.569
Who is the rightful Encolo Chief of the Kukwana?

00:01:47.629 --> 00:01:50.204
You are Encolo Chief Gagul.

00:01:50.264 --> 00:01:58.023
You see, Umbapa, even your uncle is a faithful servant to the new Enkulu chief.

00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:01.276
So now, you have a choice.

00:02:01.336 --> 00:02:06.299
Accept me as your Enkulu chief, or die.

00:02:06.319 --> 00:02:09.542
I will never accept you as my leader.

00:02:09.602 --> 00:02:13.004
You are not even a descendant of a chief.

00:02:13.064 --> 00:02:15.712
Kukwana Amazulu.

00:02:15.772 --> 00:02:19.072
Brothers and sisters of the Kukwana tribe.

00:02:19.132 --> 00:02:21.146
Listen to my weds.

00:02:21.206 --> 00:02:24.650
My father did not die a natural death.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.934
Gagul poisoned him.

00:02:26.994 --> 00:02:28.576
I saw her do it.

00:02:28.636 --> 00:02:30.489
She is an evil witch.

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:32.392
Stop him!

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.554
I am on Boppa!

00:02:34.614 --> 00:02:36.466
Son of Imo too!

00:02:36.526 --> 00:02:39.490
But to Boppa, she do Imo too!

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.632
Imo too, she do Ignose!

00:02:41.692 --> 00:02:44.445
Imo too, the son of Ignose!

00:02:44.505 --> 00:02:46.938
Silent boy!

00:02:46.998 --> 00:02:48.980
I am your chief!

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.215
I am...

00:02:51.274 --> 00:02:53.659
Take him!

00:02:53.719 --> 00:02:54.190
Take him!

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:54.830
Take him!

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:55.721
Take him!

00:02:55.781 --> 00:02:56.531
Take him!

00:02:56.551 --> 00:02:57.582
Take him!

00:02:57.642 --> 00:02:58.333
Take him!

00:02:58.393 --> 00:02:58.873
Take him!

00:02:58.893 --> 00:03:00.154
Take him!

00:03:00.174 --> 00:03:00.735
Take him!

00:03:00.755 --> 00:03:01.496
Take him!

00:03:01.556 --> 00:03:02.116
Take him!

00:03:02.136 --> 00:03:03.317
Take him!

00:03:03.357 --> 00:03:05.299
Take him!

00:03:05.319 --> 00:03:05.839
Take him!

00:03:05.859 --> 00:03:07.020
Take him!

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:07.911
Take him!

00:03:07.971 --> 00:03:09.272
Take him!

00:03:09.332 --> 00:03:11.514
Take him!

00:03:11.574 --> 00:03:14.116
Take him!

00:03:14.176 --> 00:03:15.787
Take him!

00:03:15.827 --> 00:03:16.228
Take him!

00:03:16.288 --> 00:03:17.799
Take him!

00:03:17.859 --> 00:03:19.210
Take him!

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.311
Take him!

00:03:20.371 --> 00:03:20.871
Take him!

00:03:20.911 --> 00:03:21.782
Take him!

00:03:21.842 --> 00:03:23.994
The sacred mountain.

00:03:24.054 --> 00:03:29.597
Oumbapa, have you made your peace with the spirits of our ancestors?

00:03:29.657 --> 00:03:32.608
I do not need to make my peace crazy.

00:03:32.668 --> 00:03:36.530
The spirits of our ancestors are on my side.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:41.871
But I will bring the anger of the spirits down on you and all your family.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.468
Make peace with the spirits on Baba.

00:03:44.528 --> 00:03:45.309
Please!

00:03:45.369 --> 00:03:47.329
You know you must do this.

00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:49.909
If you don't, your soul will never rest.

00:03:49.969 --> 00:03:51.640
You are right, Quasi.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.220
If you kill me, my soul will never rest.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.911
I will follow you until you are dead, and then your soul will have no rest.

00:04:00.971 --> 00:04:02.232
On Baba.

00:04:02.292 --> 00:04:04.972
You are my brother's son.

00:04:05.032 --> 00:04:07.963
I know you are in Coulomb.

00:04:07.983 --> 00:04:08.723
Wait!

00:04:08.783 --> 00:04:10.087
Yes, sir.

00:04:10.147 --> 00:04:12.112
Can you hear that?

00:04:12.172 --> 00:04:16.135
It is the sound of the spirits of our ancestors.

00:04:16.195 --> 00:04:20.129
They are telling you that what you are doing is wrong.

00:04:20.189 --> 00:04:24.122
Spirits of our Kukwana ancestors.

00:04:24.182 --> 00:04:27.384
But too, Bopacha do we moto.

00:04:27.444 --> 00:04:29.967
Imo doo, chedu, no si.

00:04:30.027 --> 00:04:32.880
Ignose kukwana in kulu.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.231
Kumbabwe is shaking.

00:04:35.291 --> 00:04:46.584
You have woken the spirits in the mountain.

00:04:46.644 --> 00:04:56.334
Chrissy?

00:04:56.394 --> 00:04:59.255
Chrissy, where are you?

00:04:59.315 --> 00:05:01.476
I'm here!

00:05:01.536 --> 00:05:02.896
I will help you!

00:05:02.956 --> 00:05:03.737
No!

00:05:03.797 --> 00:05:06.098
Umbapa, leave me!

00:05:06.158 --> 00:05:06.988
Go!

00:05:07.048 --> 00:05:08.689
Save yourself!

00:05:08.748 --> 00:05:21.348
And when the spirits tell you, come back and reclaim your tribe!

00:05:21.408 --> 00:05:35.618
Ten years later, at the house of Alan Quartermain in Durban, Southern Africa.

00:05:35.678 --> 00:05:39.797
Mr. Quartermain.

00:05:39.856 --> 00:05:41.290
Yes.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:43.391
I'm sorry to disturb you.

00:05:43.451 --> 00:05:47.473
I'm Sir Henry Curtis and this is Captain Thomas Godwin.

00:05:47.533 --> 00:05:49.244
Please to meet you, Quarterman.

00:05:49.304 --> 00:05:50.806
Heard a lot about you.

00:05:50.866 --> 00:05:56.079
Mr. Quarterman, there's a matter of some importance that we wish to speak to.

00:05:56.139 --> 00:06:00.052
I'm afraid I've only this minute arrived from Cape Town.

00:06:00.112 --> 00:06:02.483
And I long journey, certainly.

00:06:02.543 --> 00:06:04.965
But we have come from London.

00:06:05.025 --> 00:06:05.895
From London?

00:06:05.955 --> 00:06:07.548
Yes.

00:06:07.607 --> 00:06:09.460
All right.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.524
Let's talk on the veranda.

00:06:11.584 --> 00:06:16.254
Florence, bring drinks for my guests.

00:06:16.314 --> 00:06:21.080
You'll have a very beautiful home, Mr. Quartermane.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:22.630
Thank you, Sir Henry.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.072
Now, would you mind telling me the reason for your visit?

00:06:26.132 --> 00:06:31.294
Before I answer that question, Mr. Quartermane, may I ask you something?

00:06:31.354 --> 00:06:36.327
About this time last year, you were in the north of Transvaal.

00:06:36.387 --> 00:06:37.228
Am I right?

00:06:37.288 --> 00:06:37.918
Yes.

00:06:37.978 --> 00:06:41.280
Near the Lukango River beyond Matabili.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.300
Yes.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:43.821
How did you know that?

00:06:43.881 --> 00:06:45.571
What were you doing there?

00:06:45.631 --> 00:06:47.122
I was hunting elephants.

00:06:47.182 --> 00:06:48.182
It's what I do.

00:06:48.242 --> 00:06:49.872
I'm an ivory trader.

00:06:49.932 --> 00:06:51.183
But I'm sorry.

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:53.053
Why all these questions?

00:06:53.113 --> 00:06:55.674
Mr. Quarterman, I will explain.

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:57.954
But one last question.

00:06:58.014 --> 00:07:03.395
Last year at Metabili, did you meet a man called George Neville?

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:05.756
George Neville.

00:07:05.816 --> 00:07:07.896
Ah, George Neville!

00:07:07.956 --> 00:07:09.257
Yes, I did.

00:07:09.317 --> 00:07:11.668
When was the last time you saw him?

00:07:11.728 --> 00:07:12.928
A year ago.

00:07:12.988 --> 00:07:14.828
At the time you're referring to.

00:07:14.888 --> 00:07:16.649
I haven't seen him since then.

00:07:16.709 --> 00:07:18.560
Do you know what happened to him?

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.651
Can I once again ask the reason for these questions?

00:07:22.711 --> 00:07:26.982
I'm here in Africa because I want to find George Neville.

00:07:27.042 --> 00:07:28.343
He is my brother.

00:07:28.402 --> 00:07:32.064
Your brother, but Neville is not his real name.

00:07:32.124 --> 00:07:35.065
His real name is George Curtis.

00:07:35.125 --> 00:07:36.136
I see.

00:07:36.196 --> 00:07:38.267
The thing is caught, Maine.

00:07:38.327 --> 00:07:45.920
George Curtis left England a year ago with a ridiculous plan to count to Africa to look for a diamond mine.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:49.812
He booked a passage to Cape Town and hasn't been heard of since.

00:07:49.871 --> 00:07:50.898
I see.

00:07:50.958 --> 00:07:52.684
Captain Godwin.

00:07:52.744 --> 00:07:55.575
What is your interest in this matter, if I may ask?

00:07:55.635 --> 00:07:58.476
George Curtis is married to my sister.

00:07:58.536 --> 00:08:04.008
He left her and their two children in England to go off from this ridiculous adventure.

00:08:04.068 --> 00:08:09.860
So, for the second time of asking, have you any idea what his plan was?

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:14.132
Well, you're right, Neville.

00:08:14.192 --> 00:08:18.423
Your brother was looking for a diamond mine.

00:08:18.483 --> 00:08:25.226
He told me he intended to search for a place which is known as King Solomon's mind.

00:08:25.286 --> 00:08:27.297
So it's true.

00:08:27.356 --> 00:08:31.838
This is what I heard, but what are King Solomon's mind?

00:08:31.898 --> 00:08:43.860
King Solomon's mind, if they exist, are said to contain more and better diamonds than any mines in Africa, or indeed the world.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:44.788
Really?

00:08:44.848 --> 00:08:46.070
Where are they?

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:47.462
Captain Godwin.

00:08:47.522 --> 00:08:54.550
If people knew the exact location of King Solomon's minds, they would have been discovered long before now.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.212
No one knows.

00:08:56.272 --> 00:08:59.671
I do know where they are said to be.

00:08:59.731 --> 00:09:00.406
Where?

00:09:00.466 --> 00:09:05.672
They are said to be in the Suleiman Mountains to the north of Matabili.

00:09:05.732 --> 00:09:07.914
And that's where the name comes from.

00:09:07.974 --> 00:09:08.966
Suleiman.

00:09:09.026 --> 00:09:10.587
Suleiman, you see?

00:09:10.647 --> 00:09:13.050
Nothing to do with King Solomon at all.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:14.001
I see.

00:09:14.061 --> 00:09:18.916
So, when you were in Matabili, you were close to these mountains?

00:09:18.976 --> 00:09:20.308
Not at all.

00:09:20.368 --> 00:09:25.132
A few miles beyond the Lukanga River, there's nothing but desert.

00:09:25.192 --> 00:09:27.744
The Kukwana Desert, it's called.

00:09:27.804 --> 00:09:31.097
The Suleiman Mountains are beyond the desert.

00:09:31.117 --> 00:09:32.098
I see.

00:09:32.158 --> 00:09:35.570
Have you ever crossed the Kukwana Desert?

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.952
Crossed the Kukwana Desert?

00:09:38.012 --> 00:09:41.435
Zhenry, only a madman would try to do that.

00:09:41.495 --> 00:09:43.196
Why, is it too big?

00:09:43.256 --> 00:09:47.920
It is indeed big, but the size of the desert is not the problem.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.324
There are other reasons too.

00:09:50.384 --> 00:09:54.926
The Kukwana Desert is named after the Kukwana tribe.

00:09:54.986 --> 00:09:59.117
The desert and the Suleiman Mountains are their homeland.

00:09:59.177 --> 00:10:05.848
They believe that the area is a spirit world inhabited by their ancestors.

00:10:05.908 --> 00:10:12.930
Mr. Quartermain, as far as you are aware, has any white man ever crossed the Kukwana Desert?

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:15.591
I only know of one.

00:10:15.651 --> 00:10:16.611
One?

00:10:16.671 --> 00:10:17.791
Who was that?

00:10:17.851 --> 00:10:20.838
A man called Jose Sylvesteri.

00:10:20.898 --> 00:10:22.166
Do you know him?

00:10:22.226 --> 00:10:23.298
I met him.

00:10:23.358 --> 00:10:25.632
Do you know where we can find him?

00:10:25.692 --> 00:10:27.784
I'm afraid he's dead.

00:10:27.844 --> 00:10:29.368
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:30.980
What happened to him?

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:35.128
Well, I will tell you what I know.

00:10:35.188 --> 00:10:44.175
About two years ago, I was at a miserable godforsaken place on the Lukanga River called Sitanda's Kral.

00:10:44.235 --> 00:10:47.427
While I was there, I fell ill.

00:10:47.487 --> 00:10:48.568
A fever.

00:10:48.628 --> 00:10:51.109
I could hardly move for three weeks.

00:10:51.169 --> 00:11:01.065
Sitanda's Kral is not a place that many white people reach, so I was surprised one day when a European was shown into my tent.

00:11:01.125 --> 00:11:05.916
It turned out he was Portuguese.

00:11:05.976 --> 00:11:10.467
Mr. Courterman!

00:11:10.527 --> 00:11:12.439
Who are you?

00:11:12.499 --> 00:11:15.042
And what do you want?

00:11:15.102 --> 00:11:17.614
My name is Jose Silvestre.

00:11:17.674 --> 00:11:20.316
What are you doing at Sitanda's Crown?

00:11:20.376 --> 00:11:21.908
I need your help.

00:11:21.968 --> 00:11:23.610
What for?

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.852
I want to find King Solomon's diamond mines.

00:11:26.912 --> 00:11:30.702
King Solomon's mines!

00:11:30.762 --> 00:11:34.230
Don't make me laugh.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:35.431
It hurts.

00:11:35.491 --> 00:11:37.712
You find the idea amusing.

00:11:37.772 --> 00:11:39.473
Of course I do.

00:11:39.533 --> 00:11:43.414
No one has ever found King Solomon's minds.

00:11:43.474 --> 00:11:45.645
They probably don't exist.

00:11:45.705 --> 00:11:48.346
This is what I believe too.

00:11:48.406 --> 00:11:54.258
Until I was given this.

00:11:54.318 --> 00:11:58.680
What was it?

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:00.271
What did he have?

00:12:00.331 --> 00:12:01.502
A map.

00:12:01.562 --> 00:12:02.996
A map.

00:12:03.056 --> 00:12:06.423
giving the location of King Solomon's minds.

00:12:06.483 --> 00:12:07.134
Yes.

00:12:07.194 --> 00:12:08.796
Did you think it was genuine?

00:12:08.856 --> 00:12:09.506
No.

00:12:09.566 --> 00:12:10.928
Of course not.

00:12:10.988 --> 00:12:12.770
Not at the time.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:23.820
Anyway, Sylvesterre could see that I was ill and that he wasn't going to persuade me to join him, so he set off with just a servant to accompany him.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:27.191
To be honest, I forgot all about him.

00:12:27.251 --> 00:12:34.997
But then, about two weeks later, there was suddenly a lot of shouting outside my tent.

00:12:35.057 --> 00:12:43.664
What's all the noise about?

00:12:43.724 --> 00:12:46.396
It is the man who was here before Massa.

00:12:46.456 --> 00:12:47.316
What?

00:12:47.376 --> 00:12:48.947
The Portuguese?

00:12:49.007 --> 00:12:50.969
I do not know Massa.

00:12:51.029 --> 00:12:52.610
What am I?

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:54.266
Are you there?

00:12:54.326 --> 00:12:56.230
What the man?

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.571
God!

00:12:57.631 --> 00:13:01.132
Sylvester, what the devil has happened to you?

00:13:01.192 --> 00:13:02.602
What the man?

00:13:02.662 --> 00:13:04.583
I was there.

00:13:04.643 --> 00:13:07.884
I saw King Solomon's minds.

00:13:07.944 --> 00:13:10.895
But the Kukwana came after me.

00:13:10.955 --> 00:13:13.126
And I had no water.

00:13:13.186 --> 00:13:14.816
But they are there.

00:13:14.876 --> 00:13:15.926
What the man?

00:13:15.986 --> 00:13:18.137
I saw them!

00:13:18.197 --> 00:13:20.568
Calm down, man.

00:13:20.628 --> 00:13:23.183
Take it easy.

00:13:23.243 --> 00:13:25.760
Oh, man.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:29.364
Sir, did he find the mines, do you think?

00:13:29.424 --> 00:13:31.496
I don't know for sure.

00:13:31.556 --> 00:13:32.046
But...

00:13:32.087 --> 00:13:32.347
But...

00:13:32.367 --> 00:13:33.138
What?

00:13:33.198 --> 00:13:36.362
In his bag, I found the map.

00:13:36.422 --> 00:13:38.444
And some diamonds.

00:13:38.504 --> 00:13:40.526
Do you have the map?

00:13:40.586 --> 00:13:41.397
Yes.

00:13:41.458 --> 00:13:43.490
Can we see it?

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:49.300
I'll go and get it.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:14:00.774
So, this is the desert and beyond the desert here are the Suleiman Mountains.

00:14:00.834 --> 00:14:10.091
According to this map, there are forests and plenty of fresh water and this mountain here is called Kong Badway.

00:14:10.151 --> 00:14:14.244
I discovered that this is Kukwana for sacred mountain.

00:14:14.305 --> 00:14:17.707
The mines seem to be somewhere on this mountain.

00:14:17.767 --> 00:14:18.978
I see.

00:14:19.038 --> 00:14:21.611
Did you show this map to my brother?

00:14:21.671 --> 00:14:24.324
No, I didn't have it with me when I met him.

00:14:24.384 --> 00:14:25.956
But did you tell him about it?

00:14:26.016 --> 00:14:26.676
Yes.

00:14:26.736 --> 00:14:29.969
And I told him what happened to Sylvesteray too.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:33.393
I told him he was mad to try and find the mines.

00:14:33.453 --> 00:14:39.980
So Henry, buy the map from Cortamine, then we can find some natives to guide us and we can get there ourselves.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.251
You think it's that easy, do you?

00:14:43.311 --> 00:14:46.041
Well, I wish you the best of luck.

00:14:46.101 --> 00:14:49.032
No, it will definitely not be easy.

00:14:49.092 --> 00:14:58.144
I know that, but one thing I do know, Mr. Quartermane, I'm sure that you are the only person who can help us find my brother.

00:14:58.204 --> 00:14:59.965
Me?

00:15:00.005 --> 00:15:09.379
I am also a very rich man, and I will pay you not just to let me have the map, but also to accompany us to the Suleiman Mountains.

00:15:09.439 --> 00:15:14.346
Sir Henry, I will accompany you on one condition.

00:15:14.406 --> 00:15:15.697
Name your condition.

00:15:15.757 --> 00:15:18.950
I have a son who lives in London.

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:21.112
He studies medicine.

00:15:21.172 --> 00:15:25.847
He depends on me for money so that he can continue his studies.

00:15:25.907 --> 00:15:32.364
If anything happens to me, I want to make sure that he completes them.

00:15:32.424 --> 00:15:33.691
So be it.

00:15:33.751 --> 00:15:38.350
I will send a telegram to my solicitor in London tomorrow.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:48.485
I will arrange that your son can complete his medical training at my expense in the event of anything happening to you, or to me.

00:15:48.545 --> 00:15:50.576
Now, will your company us?

00:15:50.636 --> 00:15:51.496
Yes.

00:15:51.556 --> 00:15:52.637
Good man.

00:15:52.657 --> 00:15:54.228
Excellent.

00:15:54.288 --> 00:15:56.999
We will start making preparations tomorrow.

00:15:57.059 --> 00:15:58.790
Leave that to me.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:03.453
I know where to get what we need and how to get the best price.

00:16:03.513 --> 00:16:05.934
But I will tell you now.

00:16:05.994 --> 00:16:14.910
We have as much chance of surviving an attempt to reach the Suleiman Mountains as that man Silvestre.

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:19.093
Good morning, Alan.

00:16:19.153 --> 00:16:20.674
Good morning, Sir Henry.

00:16:20.734 --> 00:16:22.785
How are preparations for the journey?

00:16:22.845 --> 00:16:24.676
Not good, I'm afraid.

00:16:24.736 --> 00:16:32.100
I have the wagons that we need and the provisions, but I can't find servants who are prepared to travel with us.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:40.766
I have a driver, his name is Goza, and he's a good man, but he's only prepared to come with us as far as Sitanda's crawl.

00:16:40.826 --> 00:16:43.167
He won't cross the Kukawana desert.

00:16:43.227 --> 00:16:44.098
Don't worry.

00:16:44.158 --> 00:16:45.409
I have found someone.

00:16:45.469 --> 00:16:46.740
Two men, in fact.

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:47.760
You have.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.932
Did you tell them where we are going?

00:16:49.992 --> 00:16:51.294
Yes, of course.

00:16:51.353 --> 00:16:55.266
I told them we were going to the Solomon Mountains to look for my brother.

00:16:55.326 --> 00:16:57.998
They seem like good, strong men.

00:16:58.058 --> 00:17:03.063
One of them is rather quiet, but the other is a very intelligent man.

00:17:03.123 --> 00:17:05.074
He speaks English well, too.

00:17:05.134 --> 00:17:08.577
Of course, you must have the final decision, Courtomaine.

00:17:08.637 --> 00:17:10.619
So I have brought them here this morning.

00:17:10.679 --> 00:17:11.990
Here, yes.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.890
They are waiting outside.

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:16.611
Would you be so kind as to speak to them?

00:17:16.671 --> 00:17:21.892
Certainly.

00:17:21.952 --> 00:17:27.434
These are the men.

00:17:27.494 --> 00:17:28.474
I see.

00:17:28.534 --> 00:17:29.994
Do you speak English?

00:17:30.054 --> 00:17:31.035
Yes, Master.

00:17:31.095 --> 00:17:32.155
And you?

00:17:32.215 --> 00:17:33.846
Yes, Master.

00:17:33.906 --> 00:17:40.020
You know that we are planning to travel across the Kukawana desert and into the Solomon Mountains?

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.195
Yes, Master.

00:17:41.255 --> 00:17:42.646
We are Kukwana.

00:17:42.706 --> 00:17:44.357
We know those lands.

00:17:44.418 --> 00:17:49.352
Have you heard of the place we call King Solomon's Mines?

00:17:49.412 --> 00:17:50.592
Yes, Master.

00:17:50.653 --> 00:17:52.404
Do you know where they are?

00:17:52.464 --> 00:17:54.566
No one knows where they are, Master.

00:17:54.626 --> 00:17:55.827
I see.

00:17:55.888 --> 00:17:58.079
What are your names?

00:17:58.139 --> 00:18:00.100
This man is Kiva.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:01.392
And you?

00:18:01.452 --> 00:18:02.602
I...

00:18:02.662 --> 00:18:05.582
I am Vopa.

00:18:05.642 --> 00:18:10.501
So it was that six of us departed for the north.

00:18:10.561 --> 00:18:17.884
So Henry, Captain Godwin and myself, Goza the driver, Kiva and Umbopa.

00:18:17.944 --> 00:18:20.944
It was a journey of a thousand miles.

00:18:21.004 --> 00:18:25.966
It was the second week in March before we made camp near Sitanda's Crow.

00:18:26.026 --> 00:18:39.688
We left Goza with one wagon there and the five of us set off towards the Kukwana Desert.

00:18:39.748 --> 00:18:49.670
Umbopa and Kiva led the Oxen.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:55.004
And Sir Henry, Captain Godwin and I followed with our rifles at the ready.

00:18:55.064 --> 00:18:59.338
It was then that I noticed some marks on Umbopa's back.

00:18:59.398 --> 00:19:02.690
They looked as if they had been made with a knife.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:03.932
Umbopa?

00:19:03.992 --> 00:19:05.172
Yes, Massa.

00:19:05.232 --> 00:19:07.644
What are those marks on your back?

00:19:07.704 --> 00:19:11.198
It looks as if you had a fight with a lion.

00:19:11.258 --> 00:19:13.129
No, Massa.

00:19:13.189 --> 00:19:16.000
I don't think I would live to tell you about that.

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:24.982
Whatever the marks were, Umboper was quite clearly not planning to tell us about them.

00:19:25.042 --> 00:19:34.626
That night, we made camp near the river for the last time.

00:19:34.686 --> 00:19:41.923
The next morning, we had to turn north towards the desert.

00:19:41.984 --> 00:19:45.326
I woke early and started preparing to leave.

00:19:45.386 --> 00:19:51.010
When I went to wake the others, there was no sign of Captain Godwin.

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:52.352
Kiva!

00:19:52.412 --> 00:19:53.834
Yes, Master.

00:19:53.894 --> 00:19:56.015
Where is Captain Godwin?

00:19:56.075 --> 00:19:58.056
He went into the forest, Master.

00:19:58.116 --> 00:20:01.140
I tell him there are elephants, so he went to sea.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:02.664
Oh, my!

00:20:02.724 --> 00:20:05.348
The man's a fool.

00:20:05.408 --> 00:20:11.604
Go and find him and tell him to come back immediately.

00:20:11.664 --> 00:20:15.288
What on earth was that?

00:20:15.348 --> 00:20:16.158
I don't know.

00:20:16.178 --> 00:20:17.429
Umbopa?

00:20:17.489 --> 00:20:18.400
Yes, Musa.

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:20.982
Go and find out what is going on.

00:20:21.042 --> 00:20:28.610
Yes, Musa.

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:37.378
What in God's name is happening?

00:20:37.438 --> 00:20:40.100
I don't know, but we'd better find out.

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:41.211
Come on.

00:20:41.271 --> 00:20:48.516
Sir Henry and I began running in the direction of the noise.

00:20:48.576 --> 00:20:55.490
It was clear that Sir Henry hadn't run anywhere for a while.

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:58.132
I was soon a long way ahead of him.

00:20:58.192 --> 00:21:00.988
Then I saw Godwin running towards me.

00:21:01.048 --> 00:21:04.164
Godwin, what the hell is going on?

00:21:04.184 --> 00:21:07.797
I shot an elephant.

00:21:07.857 --> 00:21:10.830
You did what?

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:13.122
I couldn't stop myself.

00:21:13.182 --> 00:21:14.894
It was feeding.

00:21:14.954 --> 00:21:19.237
It was a sitting target, but I only wounded it.

00:21:19.297 --> 00:21:21.298
You fool!

00:21:21.358 --> 00:21:25.689
He made a dreadful noise and ran towards me.

00:21:25.749 --> 00:21:27.796
Then Kiva arrived.

00:21:27.856 --> 00:21:31.758
He started shouting and running across the elephant's path.

00:21:31.778 --> 00:21:34.619
It turned and went for here.

00:21:34.679 --> 00:21:37.880
He tore him to pieces.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:38.880
I'm sorry.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:44.122
I think he's dead.

00:21:44.142 --> 00:21:46.163
Nubari Kiva in the forest.

00:21:46.223 --> 00:21:49.364
Umbulpur said a few words in Kukwana.

00:21:49.424 --> 00:21:53.124
Then turned and spoke to us.

00:21:53.184 --> 00:21:57.406
Kiva was the bravest of brave men.

00:21:57.466 --> 00:21:58.986
Here, here.

00:21:59.047 --> 00:22:02.619
Captain Godwin, Kiva saved your life.

00:22:02.679 --> 00:22:05.290
But you have done something very bad.

00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:06.702
I know that.

00:22:06.762 --> 00:22:08.633
It is worse than you think.

00:22:08.693 --> 00:22:12.085
Kiva was a Kukwana and you caused his death.

00:22:12.145 --> 00:22:14.646
We are already on Kukwana land.

00:22:14.706 --> 00:22:17.228
You have raised the spirits of our ancestors.

00:22:17.288 --> 00:22:26.566
You must not anger the spirits again.

00:22:26.626 --> 00:22:37.204
Later that day, we finally reached the Kukwana Desert.

00:22:37.264 --> 00:22:43.776
It stretched out in front of us, crossing it seemed an impossible and foolish task.

00:22:43.836 --> 00:22:49.217
After three days, we could see the mountains in the distance.

00:22:49.257 --> 00:22:52.568
Then, on the fourth day...

00:22:52.628 --> 00:22:56.260
Sir Henry, call to men.

00:22:56.320 --> 00:22:57.602
Look!

00:22:57.662 --> 00:22:59.515
What is it, Godwin?

00:22:59.575 --> 00:23:00.516
Look!

00:23:00.576 --> 00:23:02.137
Street ahead!

00:23:02.197 --> 00:23:03.358
Trees!

00:23:03.418 --> 00:23:05.010
Thank God!

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:07.232
Trees means water!

00:23:07.292 --> 00:23:10.714
In less than an hour, we reached the trees.

00:23:10.774 --> 00:23:15.708
The good news was that there was a small lake and a forest beyond it.

00:23:15.768 --> 00:23:22.602
We all threw ourselves into the water, drinking and washing the sand off our faces.

00:23:22.662 --> 00:23:28.182
The bad news was that we were not alone.

00:23:28.242 --> 00:23:32.294
Godwin was the first to notice that we were being watched.

00:23:32.355 --> 00:23:38.198
On the edge of the forest stood a group of natives, about 30 of them.

00:23:38.258 --> 00:23:44.092
Most of them were carrying Asagai, the spears that make them such frightening warriors.

00:23:44.152 --> 00:23:53.158
One of them shouted something, and as one, they charged towards us.

00:23:53.218 --> 00:24:00.304
Godwin ran to the wagon and picked up a rifle.

00:24:00.364 --> 00:24:02.365
Stop or I shoot!

00:24:02.425 --> 00:24:08.360
The natives had clearly never seen a rifle before, so they didn't stop charging towards us.

00:24:08.420 --> 00:24:11.622
Then...

00:24:11.683 --> 00:24:17.425
One of them fell to the ground, wounded.

00:24:17.485 --> 00:24:24.377
The other stopped, then began to charge again.

00:24:24.437 --> 00:24:35.241
I thought we were all as good as dead, but then Umbopa stepped in front of the natives and began shouting at them.

00:24:35.301 --> 00:24:39.474
To my amazement, they stopped and listened to him.

00:24:39.534 --> 00:24:51.646
Kukurana Amazulu, Echata, Bhatuumbopa, Bhatuumbopa, Chedu, Imottu, Chedu Ignorci, Ignorci, Imkulu, Amazulu.

00:24:51.706 --> 00:24:54.558
Kortane, do you understand what he's saying?

00:24:54.618 --> 00:24:55.848
Not sure.

00:24:55.908 --> 00:25:03.274
I think he's telling them that he's the son of someone called Ignorci, who is the son of the great chief, Imottu.

00:25:03.334 --> 00:25:05.202
Imottu?

00:25:05.262 --> 00:25:06.098
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:06.118 --> 00:25:06.359
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:06.379 --> 00:25:06.619
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:06.639 --> 00:25:06.899
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:06.919 --> 00:25:07.160
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:07.180 --> 00:25:07.420
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:07.440 --> 00:25:07.740
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:07.760 --> 00:25:08.001
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:08.021 --> 00:25:08.261
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:08.281 --> 00:25:08.521
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:08.541 --> 00:25:08.782
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:08.802 --> 00:25:09.042
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:09.062 --> 00:25:09.322
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:09.342 --> 00:25:09.582
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:09.602 --> 00:25:09.843
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:09.863 --> 00:25:10.163
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:10.223 --> 00:25:10.524
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:10.544 --> 00:25:10.884
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:10.904 --> 00:25:11.144
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:11.164 --> 00:25:11.445
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:11.465 --> 00:25:11.705
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:11.725 --> 00:25:11.965
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:11.985 --> 00:25:12.226
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:12.246 --> 00:25:12.666
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:12.686 --> 00:25:12.926
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:12.946 --> 00:25:13.187
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:13.207 --> 00:25:13.487
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:13.507 --> 00:25:13.747
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:13.767 --> 00:25:14.028
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:14.048 --> 00:25:14.288
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:14.308 --> 00:25:14.548
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:14.568 --> 00:25:14.829
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:14.849 --> 00:25:15.109
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:15.129 --> 00:25:15.389
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:15.409 --> 00:25:15.650
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:15.670 --> 00:25:15.930
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:15.950 --> 00:25:16.210
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:16.230 --> 00:25:16.471
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:16.491 --> 00:25:16.731
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:16.771 --> 00:25:17.071
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:17.091 --> 00:25:17.352
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:17.372 --> 00:25:17.612
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:17.632 --> 00:25:17.872
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:17.892 --> 00:25:18.133
Ambaraimoto!

00:25:18.153 --> 00:25:24.872
Ambaraimoto At this point, something extraordinary happened.

00:25:24.932 --> 00:25:30.374
Umbopa turned his back on the natives, and three of them walked towards him.

00:25:30.434 --> 00:25:32.694
Godwin raised his gun again.

00:25:32.754 --> 00:25:34.115
Put your gun down.

00:25:34.175 --> 00:25:45.532
Godwin looked astonished, but did as he was told, the natives looked at the marks on Umbopa's back.

00:25:45.592 --> 00:25:53.990
to my absolute astonishment.

00:25:54.050 --> 00:26:04.333
The natives threw their asagai away and fell to the ground, as if praying at Umboper's feet.

00:26:04.393 --> 00:26:10.625
It was some time before any of us could speak.

00:26:10.685 --> 00:26:15.037
Sir Henry was the first to try to find out what was happening.

00:26:15.097 --> 00:26:18.240
Umboper, would you mind telling us what's going on?

00:26:18.300 --> 00:26:30.816
These men are Kukwana warriors, but they have been banished from their tribal home because they criticize the woman who calls herself in cool chief of the Kukwana.

00:26:30.876 --> 00:26:32.696
They are outlaws.

00:26:32.756 --> 00:26:39.436
If they go back, they will have to fight for their lives, thanks to the spirits of our ancestors.

00:26:39.496 --> 00:26:41.544
We have found each other.

00:26:41.604 --> 00:26:44.996
What do you mean, found each other?

00:26:45.057 --> 00:26:50.130
Since they were banished, they have searched these lands for their true leader.

00:26:50.190 --> 00:26:52.542
I am their true leader.

00:26:52.602 --> 00:26:53.533
You?

00:26:53.593 --> 00:26:54.574
What?

00:26:54.634 --> 00:26:57.876
I am the true chief of the Kukwana.

00:26:57.936 --> 00:27:07.998
Ten years ago, my father was killed, poisoned by an evil woman, Gagul, who now calls herself in cool chief.

00:27:08.058 --> 00:27:10.293
She tried to kill me too.

00:27:10.353 --> 00:27:13.615
But the spirits of our ancestors know this.

00:27:13.675 --> 00:27:16.346
And these men know this story too.

00:27:16.406 --> 00:27:18.587
They have been searching for me.

00:27:18.648 --> 00:27:21.860
Pardon me for doubting you, Baba.

00:27:21.920 --> 00:27:25.491
But how do these men know that you are their chief?

00:27:25.552 --> 00:27:28.333
Because of the marks on my back.

00:27:28.393 --> 00:27:31.375
Only the son of a chief has these marks.

00:27:31.435 --> 00:27:33.976
Now these men will follow and obey me.

00:27:34.036 --> 00:27:35.447
And I must lead them.

00:27:35.507 --> 00:27:36.468
Lead them?

00:27:36.528 --> 00:27:37.539
Where?

00:27:37.599 --> 00:27:42.634
It is time for me to take my place, as in Kulu chief of my tribe.

00:27:42.694 --> 00:27:45.476
They have a leader who is not the true in Kulu.

00:27:45.536 --> 00:27:49.350
I must fight her men in battle, and defeat them.

00:27:49.410 --> 00:27:54.293
Tomorrow, we will leave to do battle with Gagur and her men.

00:27:54.353 --> 00:27:56.926
Leave, but what about us?

00:27:56.986 --> 00:28:00.748
You promised to help us find George Curtis.

00:28:00.808 --> 00:28:02.810
No, Captain Daudwing.

00:28:02.870 --> 00:28:06.266
I promised to lead you to the Suleiman Mountains.

00:28:06.327 --> 00:28:08.330
This I have done.

00:28:08.390 --> 00:28:11.191
I have also saved all of your lives.

00:28:11.251 --> 00:28:13.932
Without me, you would all be dead now.

00:28:13.992 --> 00:28:15.943
Thomas, please.

00:28:16.003 --> 00:28:18.854
For once in your life, listen.

00:28:18.914 --> 00:28:25.296
Umbapa, I understand what you want to do, but we still need your help.

00:28:25.356 --> 00:28:30.077
We have to find King Solomon's minds and see if my brother is there.

00:28:30.137 --> 00:28:34.438
I need to know if he came here and if anyone saw him.

00:28:34.498 --> 00:28:35.868
Wait.

00:28:35.928 --> 00:28:40.650
I will talk to my people.

00:28:40.710 --> 00:28:46.212
After some minutes, he returned.

00:28:46.272 --> 00:28:50.994
Sir Henry, I asked the men if they had seen a white man here.

00:28:51.054 --> 00:28:52.696
What did they say?

00:28:52.756 --> 00:28:55.096
Use your brother, a tall man.

00:28:55.156 --> 00:28:57.258
Yes, very tall.

00:28:57.317 --> 00:29:00.162
A tall white man was here last year.

00:29:00.222 --> 00:29:03.738
He had one finger missing from this hand.

00:29:03.798 --> 00:29:05.529
He's left hand.

00:29:05.589 --> 00:29:07.240
Yes, that's right.

00:29:07.300 --> 00:29:08.532
It's George.

00:29:08.592 --> 00:29:10.122
Where did they see him?

00:29:10.183 --> 00:29:11.504
Where did he go?

00:29:11.564 --> 00:29:14.636
They think he was captured by Gagua's man.

00:29:14.696 --> 00:29:16.898
Oh, God, no.

00:29:16.958 --> 00:29:18.869
And then what?

00:29:18.929 --> 00:29:23.752
They took him to Kongbabwe, the tall mountain you can see over there.

00:29:23.812 --> 00:29:27.004
Kongbabwe, sacred mountain.

00:29:27.064 --> 00:29:28.938
That's where the mines are.

00:29:28.998 --> 00:29:31.692
Bopper, we must go there.

00:29:31.752 --> 00:29:33.603
Very well.

00:29:33.663 --> 00:29:38.556
But you must know that Kong Babwe is a sacred place for us.

00:29:38.616 --> 00:29:42.208
It is the resting place of the spirits of our chiefs.

00:29:42.269 --> 00:29:44.920
It is dangerous for you to go there.

00:29:44.981 --> 00:29:49.994
When the spirits are angry, Kong Babwe also becomes angry.

00:29:50.054 --> 00:29:51.976
But we have to go there.

00:29:52.036 --> 00:29:55.408
We have to find out what happened to my brother.

00:29:55.468 --> 00:29:59.068
You will never find your way to Kong Babwe alone.

00:29:59.128 --> 00:30:01.578
You will get lost in the forest.

00:30:01.638 --> 00:30:04.530
I will tell one of the men to go with you.

00:30:04.590 --> 00:30:08.952
This man is my father's brother.

00:30:09.012 --> 00:30:10.472
His name is Quesi.

00:30:10.532 --> 00:30:14.504
So he is also a descendant of the great chief Imottu.

00:30:14.564 --> 00:30:18.576
He will lead you to Kong Babu and Kona Suleiman.

00:30:18.636 --> 00:30:20.277
Kona Suleiman.

00:30:20.337 --> 00:30:22.238
Suleiman Cave.

00:30:22.298 --> 00:30:25.790
The place you call King Solomon's minds.

00:30:25.850 --> 00:30:27.099
So...

00:30:27.159 --> 00:30:34.672
You know where it is.

00:30:34.732 --> 00:30:45.968
The next morning, we set off through the dense tropical forest, towards Gangbabwe.

00:30:46.029 --> 00:30:49.531
There was no path, and the walk was hard.

00:30:49.591 --> 00:30:51.743
But Quasie knew the way.

00:30:51.803 --> 00:30:57.037
We walked for hours, until we found ourselves at the foot of the mountain.

00:30:57.097 --> 00:31:00.799
After a short rest, we began to climb.

00:31:00.860 --> 00:31:05.540
Suddenly, Quasie stopped in front of a pile of rocks.

00:31:05.600 --> 00:31:07.619
This is Konasulima.

00:31:07.679 --> 00:31:08.900
Please help me.

00:31:08.960 --> 00:31:12.532
Kuezi indicated that we had to move the rocks.

00:31:12.592 --> 00:31:14.862
So we all began to pull at them.

00:31:14.922 --> 00:31:18.154
They were large rocks and it was hard work.

00:31:18.214 --> 00:31:21.926
Eventually we could see a dark cave.

00:31:21.986 --> 00:31:24.948
It's time to light the torches.

00:31:25.009 --> 00:31:28.840
We lit torches and walked into the cave.

00:31:28.900 --> 00:31:35.481
It was dark and damp and looked like any other cave.

00:31:35.541 --> 00:31:39.410
We walked further and further.

00:31:39.470 --> 00:31:44.514
Then suddenly, the light from the torches began to reflect on...

00:31:44.574 --> 00:31:46.534
diamonds.

00:31:46.594 --> 00:31:48.786
Hundreds of them.

00:31:48.846 --> 00:31:55.019
Some were on the ground, others were still in the rock on the walls of the cave.

00:31:55.080 --> 00:31:57.290
My God!

00:31:57.350 --> 00:31:59.522
Look at all these diamonds!

00:31:59.582 --> 00:32:03.094
We have to take some of them with us, Courtman.

00:32:03.154 --> 00:32:06.392
Courtman, where are you?

00:32:06.452 --> 00:32:11.561
I had walked on ahead of the others, and I saw something.

00:32:11.621 --> 00:32:13.152
I'm over here.

00:32:13.212 --> 00:32:16.382
Sir Henry, I think you should come here.

00:32:16.442 --> 00:32:18.443
I'm coming.

00:32:18.503 --> 00:32:20.764
What is it?

00:32:20.824 --> 00:32:22.054
Look.

00:32:22.114 --> 00:32:23.274
Where?

00:32:23.334 --> 00:32:24.975
What can you see?

00:32:25.035 --> 00:32:26.605
Down below.

00:32:26.665 --> 00:32:27.716
Down there.

00:32:27.776 --> 00:32:28.456
Look.

00:32:28.516 --> 00:32:30.526
There's something there.

00:32:30.586 --> 00:32:32.937
I can't see anything.

00:32:32.997 --> 00:32:34.227
I think.

00:32:34.287 --> 00:32:35.488
I think.

00:32:35.548 --> 00:32:36.824
It's a skeleton.

00:32:36.884 --> 00:32:38.160
A skeleton.

00:32:38.221 --> 00:32:39.772
Dear God.

00:32:39.832 --> 00:32:44.534
I'll climb down and have a closer look.

00:32:44.594 --> 00:32:48.376
Be careful, Godwin.

00:32:48.436 --> 00:32:50.798
The rocks look dangerous.

00:32:50.858 --> 00:32:53.408
I'm all right.

00:32:53.468 --> 00:32:56.190
Oh my God.

00:32:56.250 --> 00:32:59.972
It is a skeleton and...

00:33:00.032 --> 00:33:04.992
So Henry, I'm afraid it's bad news.

00:33:05.052 --> 00:33:08.331
There is no middle finger on the left hand.

00:33:08.391 --> 00:33:09.652
It's George.

00:33:09.712 --> 00:33:11.193
Oh, no.

00:33:11.253 --> 00:33:15.295
Please, God, I hope his death wasn't too violent.

00:33:15.355 --> 00:33:17.576
Quartering, do you think we can...

00:33:17.636 --> 00:33:17.896
Shh!

00:33:17.916 --> 00:33:18.616
Quiet!

00:33:18.676 --> 00:33:20.127
Listen!

00:33:20.188 --> 00:33:22.919
What on earth is that noise?

00:33:22.979 --> 00:33:24.950
It's an earth tremor.

00:33:25.010 --> 00:33:25.770
Quick!

00:33:25.830 --> 00:33:27.920
We have to get out!

00:33:27.980 --> 00:33:30.250
What's happening?

00:33:30.310 --> 00:33:32.673
Godwin, it's an earth tremor!

00:33:32.733 --> 00:33:33.944
Time back up!

00:33:34.004 --> 00:33:35.796
We have to get out!

00:33:35.856 --> 00:33:37.619
I can't hear you!

00:33:37.679 --> 00:33:45.558
Look out!

00:33:45.618 --> 00:33:53.236
What's happening?

00:33:53.296 --> 00:33:55.298
I can't see a thing.

00:33:55.358 --> 00:33:57.519
There was a rock form.

00:33:57.580 --> 00:33:59.341
God wins buried.

00:33:59.401 --> 00:34:01.633
We must try to get him out of there.

00:34:01.693 --> 00:34:03.014
Are you mad?

00:34:03.074 --> 00:34:05.686
Tons of rock just fell on him.

00:34:05.746 --> 00:34:08.489
He didn't have a chance of surviving that.

00:34:08.549 --> 00:34:10.180
We have to get out.

00:34:10.240 --> 00:34:12.762
The whole cave is falling down.

00:34:12.782 --> 00:34:18.265
Come on.

00:34:18.325 --> 00:34:25.100
The entrance to the cave is disappeared!

00:34:25.160 --> 00:34:26.072
We're trapped!

00:34:26.132 --> 00:34:28.315
We have to find another way out!

00:34:28.375 --> 00:34:29.586
But look!

00:34:29.646 --> 00:34:30.788
Over there!

00:34:30.848 --> 00:34:33.532
There's a kind of tunnel in the rock!

00:34:33.593 --> 00:34:36.252
It may be a way out there!

00:34:36.312 --> 00:34:42.324
I put down my torch and began to crawl into the dark tunnel of rock.

00:34:42.384 --> 00:34:47.777
It was a small space, and as I crawled through it, it got even narrower.

00:34:47.837 --> 00:34:54.131
I felt like a rat in a drainpipe, and I was beginning to panic.

00:34:54.191 --> 00:34:55.962
But I could breathe.

00:34:56.022 --> 00:34:58.604
Air was coming from somewhere.

00:34:58.664 --> 00:35:05.306
The space began to get wider, and soon I was able to stand up.

00:35:05.366 --> 00:35:10.106
In front of me, there was another entrance to the cave.

00:35:10.167 --> 00:35:13.898
Soon Sir Henry emerged from the tunnel behind me.

00:35:13.958 --> 00:35:21.992
We were safe.

00:35:22.052 --> 00:35:29.832
God be praised.

00:35:29.892 --> 00:35:31.872
Well done, Courtney.

00:35:31.932 --> 00:35:34.764
I thought we were going to die in there, Sanri.

00:35:34.784 --> 00:35:37.716
I think we are still in trouble.

00:35:37.776 --> 00:35:38.626
What?

00:35:38.687 --> 00:35:39.668
Why?

00:35:39.728 --> 00:35:40.898
Look!

00:35:40.958 --> 00:35:45.242
Outside the cave, there was a band of natives.

00:35:45.302 --> 00:35:48.364
But they were not Umbopa's warriors.

00:35:48.424 --> 00:35:52.388
Leading them was a tall, fierce woman.

00:35:52.448 --> 00:35:59.581
I realized to my horror that we must be in the presence of the evil chief, Gagul.

00:35:59.641 --> 00:36:01.490
white men.

00:36:01.550 --> 00:36:08.284
You have entered the Kona Solomon, and you have woken the anger of our ancestors.

00:36:08.344 --> 00:36:11.206
You will die for this.

00:36:11.266 --> 00:36:13.087
Kill them!"

00:36:13.148 --> 00:36:15.889
There seemed no way to escape now.

00:36:15.909 --> 00:36:20.702
I was convinced that these were the last moments of my life.

00:36:20.762 --> 00:36:28.725
But then, suddenly, Umbopa appeared behind Gagul, alone.

00:36:28.785 --> 00:36:32.025
Agua!

00:36:32.085 --> 00:36:35.147
Who are you?

00:36:35.207 --> 00:36:42.081
I am Umbapa, in Kulu chief of the Kukwana.

00:36:42.141 --> 00:36:43.471
Umbapa?

00:36:43.532 --> 00:36:45.403
Impossible!

00:36:45.463 --> 00:36:47.664
Umbapa is dead!

00:36:47.725 --> 00:36:49.536
No, Gagua.

00:36:49.596 --> 00:36:54.246
You killed my father, but you could not kill me.

00:36:54.306 --> 00:36:59.148
The spirit saved me and brought me back here to defeat you.

00:36:59.208 --> 00:37:02.030
You will never defeat me!

00:37:02.050 --> 00:37:05.092
No one will defeat me!

00:37:05.152 --> 00:37:06.453
Kill him!

00:37:06.514 --> 00:37:08.546
Now!

00:37:08.606 --> 00:37:12.809
Before Gagun's men could meet Chumbopa.

00:37:12.869 --> 00:37:17.085
Crazy and the other outlaws appeared behind them.

00:37:17.145 --> 00:37:24.480
Gagul's men were taken by surprise, and were killed or taken prisoner almost immediately.

00:37:24.540 --> 00:37:32.622
Two of Umboper's warriors held Gagul, and another was about to drive an Asagai through her heart.

00:37:32.682 --> 00:37:33.512
Stop!

00:37:33.572 --> 00:37:35.533
Don't kill her!

00:37:35.593 --> 00:37:42.324
Gagul, you deserve to die, because you have murdered the Inculu chief of our people.

00:37:42.384 --> 00:37:44.095
Then kill me!

00:37:44.115 --> 00:37:47.745
I am not afraid of death!

00:37:47.805 --> 00:37:48.774
No.

00:37:48.834 --> 00:37:52.266
A murder is not resolved by another murder.

00:37:52.326 --> 00:37:54.738
We will go back to our homeland.

00:37:54.798 --> 00:37:59.020
And we will both face the justice of the Kukwana people.

00:37:59.080 --> 00:38:03.742
They will decide who they want to be, they in Kulu chief.

00:38:03.803 --> 00:38:06.044
Me or you?

00:38:06.104 --> 00:38:07.515
Take her away.

00:38:07.575 --> 00:38:09.036
I will join you later.

00:38:09.096 --> 00:38:10.947
Yes, sir.

00:38:11.007 --> 00:38:14.889
Sir Henry, you have been into Kona Suleiman.

00:38:14.949 --> 00:38:16.906
What did you find there?

00:38:16.966 --> 00:38:19.724
We found the body of my brother.

00:38:19.784 --> 00:38:21.544
I am sorry.

00:38:21.604 --> 00:38:23.795
And where is Captain Godwin?

00:38:23.855 --> 00:38:26.316
He was killed by a rockfall.

00:38:26.376 --> 00:38:30.017
You are a noble and a brave man, Sir Henry.

00:38:30.077 --> 00:38:32.097
You did what you had to do.

00:38:32.157 --> 00:38:33.228
Did I?

00:38:33.288 --> 00:38:34.890
I don't know.

00:38:34.950 --> 00:38:38.986
Of course I mean, I want to leave this place immediately.

00:38:39.046 --> 00:38:41.018
We must return to Dublin.

00:38:41.078 --> 00:38:44.161
How do you propose to do that, Sir Henry?

00:38:44.221 --> 00:38:48.926
You forget that we have no provisions and no one to guide us.

00:38:48.986 --> 00:38:55.032
I told you that only a fool would try to find King Solomon's mind.

00:38:55.092 --> 00:38:58.124
There must be some way we can get back.

00:38:58.184 --> 00:39:07.178
If you can think of a way we can do that, then please tell me, because I have no idea how we will do it.

00:39:07.238 --> 00:39:10.300
We will help you to return to Durban.

00:39:10.360 --> 00:39:12.752
I will send five men with you.

00:39:12.812 --> 00:39:20.958
They will make sure you have food to eat, and they will protect you, until you reach Sitalas Krah.

00:39:21.018 --> 00:39:36.377
We made our way slowly and wearily back to Durban, and we were almost dead with exhaustion when we finally reached my house.

00:39:36.437 --> 00:39:45.371
Sehenry rested for a few days and returned home to England.

00:39:45.432 --> 00:39:50.417
When he left, I decided to write this account of what happened.

00:39:50.477 --> 00:39:54.972
I have seen the legendary King Solomon's minds.

00:39:55.032 --> 00:39:58.984
My son's future as a doctor is secure.

00:39:59.044 --> 00:40:05.936
But my health is not good, and I don't expect to live much longer.

00:40:05.996 --> 00:40:13.640
Let this serve as a warning to anyone else who tries to find King Solomon's minds.

00:40:13.700 --> 00:40:34.924
You may not live to tell the tale.

00:40:34.984 --> 00:41:17.399
The White Lion How am I going to carry this water all the way to the village?

00:41:17.459 --> 00:41:20.352
I'm not surprised you have a pain in your back, Jata.

00:41:20.412 --> 00:41:23.736
It's all that time you spend lying down.

00:41:23.796 --> 00:41:27.610
That's such a bad thing to say.

00:41:27.670 --> 00:41:29.992
Be happy, Jata.

00:41:30.053 --> 00:41:35.328
Your husband is our chief, a great man, and he loves you.

00:41:35.388 --> 00:41:40.132
If one zero really loved me, he would carry this bucket for me.

00:41:40.192 --> 00:41:42.986
No man would do that for a woman.

00:41:43.046 --> 00:41:44.897
Men are lazy.

00:41:44.957 --> 00:41:46.808
You are like Mumbi.

00:41:46.868 --> 00:41:48.520
All men are lazy.

00:41:48.580 --> 00:41:51.853
But your husband is a lion among men.

00:41:51.913 --> 00:41:53.944
He looks after us well.

00:41:54.004 --> 00:41:55.836
Everyone loves him.

00:41:55.897 --> 00:41:58.038
Everyone except Chumbo.

00:41:58.098 --> 00:42:00.080
Chumbo, true.

00:42:00.140 --> 00:42:03.372
The medicine man is jealous of your husband.

00:42:03.432 --> 00:42:05.214
Everyone knows that.

00:42:05.274 --> 00:42:06.794
He wants to be Chief.

00:42:06.854 --> 00:42:08.454
Yes.

00:42:08.514 --> 00:42:10.345
Don't worry, Jata.

00:42:10.405 --> 00:42:12.766
It will never happen.

00:42:12.826 --> 00:42:15.656
Wangiro is Chief for Life.

00:42:15.716 --> 00:42:18.817
Chiambo will never be Chief.

00:42:18.877 --> 00:42:19.638
Come.

00:42:19.698 --> 00:42:21.960
Let's go back.

00:42:22.020 --> 00:42:25.512
You know they are meeting this afternoon.

00:42:25.532 --> 00:42:26.542
Who?

00:42:26.602 --> 00:42:29.633
The chief, Tumbor and the other elders.

00:42:29.693 --> 00:42:30.624
Why?

00:42:30.684 --> 00:42:33.615
They will talk about Wanjiro's idea.

00:42:33.675 --> 00:42:35.185
Oh, yes.

00:42:35.245 --> 00:42:37.626
The nature reserve.

00:42:37.686 --> 00:42:39.667
I don't understand.

00:42:39.727 --> 00:42:44.258
Around the village, there is land, there are animals.

00:42:44.319 --> 00:42:48.230
What is the difference if it is called a nature reserve?

00:42:48.290 --> 00:42:53.866
If it becomes a nature reserve, it means that the land will be protected.

00:42:53.926 --> 00:42:57.189
There will be wardens in Land Rover cars.

00:42:57.249 --> 00:43:00.993
They will make sure that poachers are kept off the land.

00:43:01.053 --> 00:43:03.286
But who will pay for all this?

00:43:03.346 --> 00:43:11.414
The aid development organization, it is an international organization which helps to improve our lives.

00:43:11.474 --> 00:43:15.456
Do you remember the white people who came to the village last month?

00:43:15.516 --> 00:43:16.837
Yes.

00:43:16.897 --> 00:43:18.788
Now I remember.

00:43:18.848 --> 00:43:22.961
So, do you think the Nature Reserve idea is a good one?

00:43:23.021 --> 00:43:24.672
Yes, I do.

00:43:24.732 --> 00:43:26.784
But Chumbo is against it.

00:43:26.844 --> 00:43:27.334
Why?

00:43:27.354 --> 00:43:32.257
These days, he is against everything that Wanjiro suggests.

00:43:32.317 --> 00:43:39.536
Paul and Giro, he tries so hard to be understanding and fair to everyone.

00:43:39.596 --> 00:43:43.420
But Chumbo makes that so difficult for him.

00:43:43.480 --> 00:43:44.622
And look!

00:43:44.682 --> 00:43:45.853
What is it?

00:43:45.914 --> 00:43:47.275
A cow!

00:43:47.335 --> 00:43:51.295
Lion would be past!

00:43:51.355 --> 00:43:55.904
It is Echinia's cow.

00:43:55.964 --> 00:43:57.364
Dead?

00:43:57.424 --> 00:43:59.394
Oh no.

00:43:59.455 --> 00:44:01.825
Poor Echinia.

00:44:01.885 --> 00:44:04.856
But how was it killed?

00:44:04.916 --> 00:44:07.887
Look at those marks on its neck.

00:44:07.947 --> 00:44:11.278
It looks as if it was attacked by a lion.

00:44:11.338 --> 00:44:14.078
But when did this happen?

00:44:14.138 --> 00:44:17.920
It was not here when we came to the well three hours ago.

00:44:17.980 --> 00:44:29.521
We must warn the village.

00:44:29.581 --> 00:44:42.183
Why must you always oppose me, Chumbo?

00:44:42.243 --> 00:44:46.875
Whatever I say, I can be sure you will suggest the opposite.

00:44:46.935 --> 00:44:51.567
It pleases you to say that when you are zero, but it is not true.

00:44:51.627 --> 00:44:52.818
Not true.

00:44:52.878 --> 00:44:56.809
Why are you against the idea of a nature reserve?

00:44:56.869 --> 00:44:58.570
It is perfect for us.

00:44:58.630 --> 00:45:05.092
It will protect our land and our animals, both the animals of the village and the animals in the wild.

00:45:05.152 --> 00:45:08.284
It will stop the poachers who are a real problem.

00:45:08.344 --> 00:45:13.256
I am tired of hearing of dead elephants killed for their tusks.

00:45:13.316 --> 00:45:14.246
I agree.

00:45:14.306 --> 00:45:16.286
The poachers must be stopped.

00:45:16.346 --> 00:45:17.748
You agree?

00:45:17.808 --> 00:45:21.634
You agree with something I say, I'm amazed.

00:45:21.694 --> 00:45:24.720
There are other ways we can stop them.

00:45:24.780 --> 00:45:27.624
We do not need a nature reserve.

00:45:27.685 --> 00:45:29.568
Yes, we do.

00:45:29.628 --> 00:45:31.990
It is the best thing for us.

00:45:32.050 --> 00:45:38.074
We need trained people who can patrol our land and keep our animals safe from poachers.

00:45:38.134 --> 00:45:43.818
We can patrol the land ourselves, but there is no need to make our land a nature reserve.

00:45:43.879 --> 00:45:48.702
If we do that, we have to deal with the air development organization.

00:45:48.762 --> 00:45:50.103
White people.

00:45:50.163 --> 00:45:53.376
White people do not understand our way of life.

00:45:53.436 --> 00:45:58.140
They will force us to do things their way, not our way.

00:45:58.200 --> 00:46:00.492
You are wrong, Chumbo.

00:46:00.552 --> 00:46:04.374
I had a meeting with the aid development people last week.

00:46:04.434 --> 00:46:06.746
They want nothing from us.

00:46:06.806 --> 00:46:11.160
They will give us money and let us make our own decisions.

00:46:11.220 --> 00:46:14.272
They will find some way to control us.

00:46:14.332 --> 00:46:16.534
What is your feeling, Bruno?

00:46:16.594 --> 00:46:18.475
I agree with you, One Zero.

00:46:18.535 --> 00:46:19.415
Of course you do.

00:46:19.475 --> 00:46:21.396
You are One Zero's footstool.

00:46:21.456 --> 00:46:23.687
I will not forgive you for that, Jumbo.

00:46:23.747 --> 00:46:25.888
I am shaking with Theo, Runo.

00:46:25.948 --> 00:46:28.419
Murithi, you've said nothing at all.

00:46:28.479 --> 00:46:30.010
What is your opinion?

00:46:30.070 --> 00:46:32.350
I agree with you, Jumbo.

00:46:32.410 --> 00:46:37.085
I'm afraid the aid development people will control us.

00:46:37.145 --> 00:46:41.210
We'll call a meeting of the whole village.

00:46:41.270 --> 00:46:47.624
You will find Chumbo that most people are in favor of the idea of a nature reserve.

00:46:47.685 --> 00:46:51.357
They will not be after they hear me speak.

00:46:51.417 --> 00:46:53.188
We shall see.

00:46:53.248 --> 00:46:59.122
Now, this cow that was found this morning on the path to the well, who has seen it?

00:46:59.182 --> 00:47:00.864
Moombi took me to see it.

00:47:00.924 --> 00:47:03.415
It looks as if it was killed by a lion.

00:47:03.475 --> 00:47:06.374
But it didn't eat any part of the cow.

00:47:06.434 --> 00:47:09.333
Hmm, that is strange.

00:47:09.394 --> 00:47:11.605
This lion must be ill.

00:47:11.666 --> 00:47:14.558
We'll have to send out a search party to find it.

00:47:14.618 --> 00:47:16.580
Runo, will you lead it?

00:47:16.640 --> 00:47:18.032
Of course, Wangeer.

00:47:18.092 --> 00:47:19.252
Good.

00:47:19.312 --> 00:47:21.574
The meeting is ended.

00:47:21.634 --> 00:47:23.807
Chief Wangeer, wait!

00:47:23.867 --> 00:47:25.398
What is it, Murethi?

00:47:25.458 --> 00:47:27.870
Chomo is in a trance.

00:47:27.930 --> 00:47:32.054
We must listen to his words.

00:47:32.114 --> 00:47:36.567
I see bad things coming.

00:47:36.628 --> 00:47:40.150
Many bad things are tribe is in danger.

00:47:40.210 --> 00:47:42.701
I said the meeting is ended.

00:47:42.761 --> 00:47:43.822
What?

00:47:43.882 --> 00:47:44.922
Ended?

00:47:44.982 --> 00:47:46.924
Have you no respect for me?

00:47:46.984 --> 00:47:52.347
I am the medicine man and you must listen when I speak.

00:47:52.407 --> 00:47:58.288
When you talk sense, then I will listen.

00:47:58.348 --> 00:48:11.071
He does not yet understand the power of magic, but he will.

00:48:11.131 --> 00:48:16.694
Umbogo!

00:48:16.754 --> 00:48:18.205
Umbogo!

00:48:18.265 --> 00:48:19.716
What is it, Chige?

00:48:19.776 --> 00:48:21.606
Where are you going?

00:48:21.667 --> 00:48:23.787
Some of our cows have disappeared.

00:48:23.847 --> 00:48:25.476
I have to find them.

00:48:25.536 --> 00:48:27.526
I will come with you.

00:48:27.586 --> 00:48:29.818
Why are you carrying a gun?

00:48:29.878 --> 00:48:31.429
Because of the lion.

00:48:31.490 --> 00:48:32.780
The lion?

00:48:32.841 --> 00:48:34.632
Are you planning to shoot it?

00:48:34.692 --> 00:48:35.733
Of course.

00:48:35.793 --> 00:48:38.275
Then I will be a hero in the village.

00:48:38.335 --> 00:48:42.398
And the lovely matter will fall in love with me.

00:48:42.458 --> 00:48:47.370
Seriously, in Bogo, this is not a good idea.

00:48:47.430 --> 00:48:53.590
You know you have to get permission from my father when zero before you kill a lion.

00:48:53.650 --> 00:48:55.031
I know that.

00:48:55.091 --> 00:48:58.134
I will only kill the lion if it attacks him.

00:48:58.194 --> 00:48:59.504
I am not stupid.

00:48:59.564 --> 00:49:02.466
We will have to be careful, of course.

00:49:02.527 --> 00:49:05.078
But we also have to find the cows.

00:49:05.138 --> 00:49:06.920
How many are missing?

00:49:06.980 --> 00:49:07.780
Three.

00:49:07.840 --> 00:49:08.811
Check it.

00:49:08.871 --> 00:49:09.712
Look.

00:49:09.772 --> 00:49:10.662
What?

00:49:10.722 --> 00:49:11.793
Over there.

00:49:11.853 --> 00:49:12.774
A cow.

00:49:12.834 --> 00:49:13.634
Where?

00:49:13.694 --> 00:49:15.375
I can't see anything.

00:49:15.436 --> 00:49:17.427
It is lying on the ground.

00:49:17.487 --> 00:49:20.578
Come on.

00:49:20.638 --> 00:49:24.399
Is it dead?

00:49:24.459 --> 00:49:25.500
Yes.

00:49:25.560 --> 00:49:26.980
And look.

00:49:27.040 --> 00:49:29.391
The others are over there.

00:49:29.451 --> 00:49:35.093
Oh no.

00:49:35.153 --> 00:49:36.794
What was that?

00:49:36.854 --> 00:49:38.314
A lion.

00:49:38.374 --> 00:49:40.074
Where is it?

00:49:40.134 --> 00:49:42.956
I don't know.

00:49:43.016 --> 00:49:45.426
The noise is coming from over there.

00:49:45.486 --> 00:49:47.860
In those bushes.

00:49:47.920 --> 00:49:50.413
We must kill it.

00:49:50.474 --> 00:49:55.517
We cannot kill a lion without the permission of my father.

00:49:55.577 --> 00:49:57.798
One zero will understand.

00:49:57.859 --> 00:50:00.100
Our animals are more important.

00:50:00.160 --> 00:50:01.181
Wait.

00:50:01.241 --> 00:50:04.553
Let me go back to the village and find him.

00:50:04.613 --> 00:50:05.554
No.

00:50:05.614 --> 00:50:06.994
Stop.

00:50:07.054 --> 00:50:08.916
I can see it.

00:50:08.976 --> 00:50:10.127
Where?

00:50:10.187 --> 00:50:11.257
There.

00:50:11.318 --> 00:50:13.038
In the bushes.

00:50:13.098 --> 00:50:15.523
I am going to shoot it.

00:50:15.583 --> 00:50:17.856
Bogo, stop!

00:50:17.917 --> 00:50:19.057
Why?

00:50:19.117 --> 00:50:20.958
The lion.

00:50:21.018 --> 00:50:23.368
I can see it now.

00:50:23.428 --> 00:50:25.369
It's white.

00:50:25.429 --> 00:50:27.390
A white lion?

00:50:27.450 --> 00:50:28.990
Are you sure?

00:50:29.050 --> 00:50:30.211
Yes.

00:50:30.271 --> 00:50:33.172
We cannot kill a white lion.

00:50:33.232 --> 00:50:37.444
We must go back and tell when zero what we have seen.

00:50:37.504 --> 00:50:38.734
Okay.

00:50:38.794 --> 00:50:40.074
Let us go.

00:50:40.134 --> 00:50:45.277
Quickly.

00:50:45.337 --> 00:50:51.070
Please, close the doors.

00:50:51.090 --> 00:50:52.470
You all know why I called this meeting.

00:50:52.510 --> 00:51:04.098
More of our animals have been killed and a lion has been seen, but a white lion.

00:51:04.158 --> 00:51:18.629
When was a white lion last seen in our land?

00:51:18.689 --> 00:51:20.600
What must we do, Juan Jiro?

00:51:20.660 --> 00:51:22.801
Please give us your commands.

00:51:22.861 --> 00:51:29.885
Even if the lion is a white lion, it must be killed.

00:51:29.945 --> 00:51:33.847
I have something to say.

00:51:33.907 --> 00:51:36.882
What is it, Tummo?

00:51:36.942 --> 00:51:40.847
We cannot kill a white lion.

00:51:40.907 --> 00:51:42.668
It is forbidden.

00:51:42.728 --> 00:51:45.410
It has come for a reason.

00:51:45.471 --> 00:51:47.692
And what is this reason?

00:51:47.752 --> 00:51:52.706
We are being punished.

00:51:52.766 --> 00:51:58.480
Why do you think we are being punished, Jumbo?

00:51:58.540 --> 00:52:00.062
I do not know.

00:52:00.122 --> 00:52:03.137
But I will find out.

00:52:03.197 --> 00:52:05.842
Please tell us what you discover.

00:52:05.902 --> 00:52:09.014
In the meantime, I have an idea.

00:52:09.074 --> 00:52:13.617
Our friends from the aid development agency can help us.

00:52:13.677 --> 00:52:15.678
I've spoken with them.

00:52:15.738 --> 00:52:21.693
If we wish, they will go out in their land rovers and look for the lion.

00:52:21.753 --> 00:52:23.864
We do not need these white men.

00:52:23.924 --> 00:52:28.799
They've helped us before and they can help us again.

00:52:28.859 --> 00:52:30.791
What do our people think?

00:52:30.851 --> 00:52:35.093
Do you agree that I should ask the development workers to do this?

00:52:35.153 --> 00:52:36.734
Yes, yes, yes.

00:52:36.754 --> 00:52:38.976
Then it's agreed.

00:52:39.036 --> 00:52:40.736
I will ask them.

00:52:40.797 --> 00:52:44.288
And if they see the lion, do not let them shoot it.

00:52:44.348 --> 00:52:46.970
You will bring disaster to our people.

00:52:47.030 --> 00:52:49.001
They will not shoot it.

00:52:49.061 --> 00:53:00.470
But we must find it before more animals are killed.

00:53:00.530 --> 00:53:10.928
Bruno, what do you want?

00:53:10.988 --> 00:53:13.098
I need to speak with you.

00:53:13.158 --> 00:53:14.209
Please.

00:53:14.269 --> 00:53:16.319
Come in.

00:53:16.380 --> 00:53:19.551
What do you want to talk to me about?

00:53:19.611 --> 00:53:22.522
You made fun of me at the last meeting.

00:53:22.582 --> 00:53:25.023
I am not happy about that.

00:53:25.083 --> 00:53:27.204
Let me apologize.

00:53:27.264 --> 00:53:29.424
Your apology is accepted.

00:53:29.484 --> 00:53:31.055
If it is real.

00:53:31.115 --> 00:53:32.076
Of course.

00:53:32.136 --> 00:53:34.276
I am a man of honor.

00:53:34.337 --> 00:53:36.449
Now tell me.

00:53:36.510 --> 00:53:38.714
Did you find the lion?

00:53:38.774 --> 00:53:39.914
No.

00:53:39.975 --> 00:53:43.308
We have searched all the forests around the village.

00:53:43.368 --> 00:53:45.110
It is very strange.

00:53:45.170 --> 00:53:49.063
There is no sign of a lion, no sign at all.

00:53:49.124 --> 00:53:51.676
And the white men in the Land Rover.

00:53:51.736 --> 00:53:53.788
They have found nothing either.

00:53:53.848 --> 00:53:57.562
There are no lions at all between here and Malindi.

00:53:57.622 --> 00:53:59.445
You will find nothing.

00:53:59.505 --> 00:54:02.436
Because this lion is a spirit.

00:54:02.496 --> 00:54:04.137
A spirit.

00:54:04.197 --> 00:54:07.117
It can be seen or not seen.

00:54:07.177 --> 00:54:09.568
Visible or invisible.

00:54:09.628 --> 00:54:15.779
And when it is seen, it is seen in different places at the same time.

00:54:15.839 --> 00:54:16.999
What?

00:54:17.059 --> 00:54:18.679
How do you know?

00:54:18.739 --> 00:54:20.679
Many people have told me.

00:54:20.740 --> 00:54:29.594
Itumu, mukami, nukjogu and gari, they all saw it at the same time yesterday.

00:54:29.654 --> 00:54:31.388
Are you sure?

00:54:31.448 --> 00:54:34.350
Do you doubt the word of a medicine man?

00:54:34.410 --> 00:54:35.290
No.

00:54:35.350 --> 00:54:36.862
Of course not.

00:54:36.922 --> 00:54:39.062
But what are we to do?

00:54:39.122 --> 00:54:42.894
We have to discover why the lion is here.

00:54:42.955 --> 00:54:45.456
Then we will know what to do.

00:54:45.516 --> 00:54:48.788
And I have a plan.

00:54:48.848 --> 00:54:51.078
Someone is here to see you.

00:54:51.138 --> 00:54:52.469
Should I leave?

00:54:52.530 --> 00:54:54.440
No, stay.

00:54:54.500 --> 00:54:57.562
I think it is Vakira, the daughter of Mumbi.

00:54:57.622 --> 00:54:59.242
Mumbi's daughter?

00:54:59.302 --> 00:55:01.983
She is only eight years old.

00:55:02.043 --> 00:55:04.054
Why is she visiting you?

00:55:04.114 --> 00:55:08.585
Small children can often see things we cannot see you know.

00:55:08.645 --> 00:55:12.686
She can help me find the answer to the mystery of the lion.

00:55:12.746 --> 00:55:14.467
Are you serious?

00:55:14.527 --> 00:55:18.544
You are going to ask a child to explain the mystery.

00:55:18.604 --> 00:55:24.464
Bruno, do not question the ways of the medicine man.

00:55:24.524 --> 00:55:30.228
Please let Vakira in and stay to listen to what she has to say.

00:55:30.288 --> 00:55:33.350
Welcome, Vakira.

00:55:33.410 --> 00:55:36.682
You want to see me, Basa?

00:55:36.742 --> 00:55:40.636
Please, sit down here.

00:55:40.696 --> 00:55:45.440
Vakira, you see this bowl of water?

00:55:45.500 --> 00:55:46.846
Yes.

00:55:46.906 --> 00:55:52.614
With it, you can help me solve the mystery of the white lion.

00:55:52.674 --> 00:55:54.364
How?

00:55:54.424 --> 00:55:58.145
Hold the ball in both hands.

00:55:58.205 --> 00:56:00.496
Look into the water.

00:56:00.556 --> 00:56:04.606
Tell me what you see.

00:56:04.667 --> 00:56:08.137
I can't see anything.

00:56:08.197 --> 00:56:10.608
Look again.

00:56:10.668 --> 00:56:14.789
Now, I can see a lion.

00:56:14.849 --> 00:56:16.250
What?

00:56:16.310 --> 00:56:19.484
What color is the lion wakira?

00:56:19.544 --> 00:56:21.154
White.

00:56:21.214 --> 00:56:24.578
Are you sure the lion is white?

00:56:24.638 --> 00:56:26.028
Yes.

00:56:26.088 --> 00:56:28.560
And he looks angry.

00:56:28.620 --> 00:56:30.032
Very angry.

00:56:30.092 --> 00:56:31.222
Wakira.

00:56:31.283 --> 00:56:34.786
Ask the lion why he is angry.

00:56:34.846 --> 00:56:37.966
Why are you angry?

00:56:38.026 --> 00:56:41.695
He is angry with the chief.

00:56:41.755 --> 00:56:43.896
Angled with the chief?

00:56:43.956 --> 00:56:45.226
Yes.

00:56:45.286 --> 00:56:48.788
He says the chief is a bad man.

00:56:48.848 --> 00:56:49.808
What?

00:56:49.868 --> 00:56:55.710
A bad man?

00:56:55.770 --> 00:57:01.472
I'm frightened.

00:57:01.532 --> 00:57:03.683
I made the lion angry.

00:57:03.743 --> 00:57:05.624
Don't worry, Akira.

00:57:05.684 --> 00:57:09.410
You have done very well.

00:57:09.470 --> 00:57:12.406
But I cannot leave.

00:57:12.466 --> 00:57:14.608
The lion is near.

00:57:14.668 --> 00:57:17.241
Wait.

00:57:17.301 --> 00:57:20.624
It is safe now.

00:57:20.684 --> 00:57:22.056
Runo.

00:57:22.116 --> 00:57:23.247
Yes?

00:57:23.307 --> 00:57:26.470
Will you take Wakiro back to her home?

00:57:26.530 --> 00:57:27.851
Of course.

00:57:27.912 --> 00:57:30.995
Thank you.

00:57:31.055 --> 00:57:36.926
Murithi, you can come in now.

00:57:36.986 --> 00:57:41.166
Is everything all right?

00:57:41.226 --> 00:57:42.226
Yes.

00:57:42.286 --> 00:57:43.577
Well done.

00:57:43.637 --> 00:57:45.157
You did well.

00:57:45.217 --> 00:57:46.798
I did my best.

00:57:46.858 --> 00:57:48.799
Where is the recording machine?

00:57:48.859 --> 00:57:49.919
Here.

00:57:49.979 --> 00:57:52.780
When it is dark, take it to the cave.

00:57:52.840 --> 00:57:54.501
We do not need it anymore.

00:57:54.561 --> 00:57:56.802
The plan is going well, Modify.

00:57:56.862 --> 00:57:59.583
But there is one thing I don't understand.

00:57:59.603 --> 00:58:02.634
Oakira saw nothing in the water.

00:58:02.694 --> 00:58:05.717
How did you persuade her to tell lies?

00:58:05.778 --> 00:58:11.602
I told her that she would grow into a beautiful woman if she helped me.

00:58:11.662 --> 00:58:14.503
Chumbo, you should not lie to a child.

00:58:14.563 --> 00:58:16.644
It is for the greater good morithi.

00:58:16.704 --> 00:58:24.887
Soon the whole village will know that the chief is a bad man and soon after that, you will be the new chief.

00:58:24.947 --> 00:58:26.868
Who is this?

00:58:26.928 --> 00:58:27.988
I don't know.

00:58:28.048 --> 00:58:29.749
We must not let them in.

00:58:29.809 --> 00:58:32.080
They must not see the recording machine.

00:58:32.140 --> 00:58:33.630
Leave by this door.

00:58:33.690 --> 00:58:34.841
Take the machine.

00:58:34.901 --> 00:58:36.696
Give it to me.

00:58:36.756 --> 00:58:39.012
Fool!

00:58:39.072 --> 00:58:40.534
Trumbol!

00:58:40.594 --> 00:58:42.044
Are you there?

00:58:42.104 --> 00:58:44.866
Quickly!

00:58:44.926 --> 00:58:47.537
Trumbol!

00:58:47.597 --> 00:58:49.088
You're here!

00:58:49.148 --> 00:58:51.419
And you, Morithi!

00:58:51.479 --> 00:58:54.330
Why didn't you answer when I called?

00:58:54.390 --> 00:59:04.391
And what is that machine?

00:59:04.451 --> 00:59:12.880
Moonby.

00:59:12.940 --> 00:59:16.042
Did you know that four cows have been killed now?

00:59:16.102 --> 00:59:16.933
Yes.

00:59:16.993 --> 00:59:20.505
Everyone is sure that a lion is responsible.

00:59:20.565 --> 00:59:22.186
A white lion.

00:59:22.246 --> 00:59:26.378
But white lions never come to this part of the country.

00:59:26.438 --> 00:59:27.069
I know.

00:59:27.129 --> 00:59:28.759
It is strange.

00:59:28.820 --> 00:59:30.721
Ojata, look.

00:59:30.781 --> 00:59:32.732
Someone is coming to the well.

00:59:32.792 --> 00:59:34.112
Who is it?

00:59:34.172 --> 00:59:36.603
I think it's Runo.

00:59:36.663 --> 00:59:39.832
Bruno, coming to the well?

00:59:39.893 --> 00:59:43.073
Maybe his wife has sent him to get water.

00:59:43.133 --> 00:59:45.794
Now that is not possible.

00:59:45.834 --> 00:59:50.654
Bruno, why are you coming to the well?

00:59:50.714 --> 00:59:54.085
Are you going to carry water home for your wife?

00:59:54.145 --> 00:59:56.795
He doesn't look very happy.

00:59:56.856 --> 01:00:01.126
Bruno, why are you looking so serious?

01:00:01.186 --> 01:00:04.227
Grata, I need to speak to you.

01:00:04.287 --> 01:00:06.596
Speak to me then.

01:00:06.656 --> 01:00:09.356
I have some bad news.

01:00:09.416 --> 01:00:11.087
What's the matter?

01:00:11.147 --> 01:00:12.628
The lion.

01:00:12.688 --> 01:00:13.938
Oh no.

01:00:13.998 --> 01:00:15.609
There are more dead animals?

01:00:15.669 --> 01:00:16.690
No.

01:00:16.750 --> 01:00:18.720
Not animals.

01:00:18.781 --> 01:00:19.851
No.

01:00:19.911 --> 01:00:21.902
What has happened then?

01:00:21.962 --> 01:00:23.233
Jada.

01:00:23.293 --> 01:00:25.364
You must please come with me.

01:00:25.424 --> 01:00:26.505
What's wrong?

01:00:26.565 --> 01:00:27.815
What's happened?

01:00:27.876 --> 01:00:30.376
The lion has killed again.

01:00:30.437 --> 01:00:32.398
But this time...

01:00:32.458 --> 01:00:33.728
This time?

01:00:33.788 --> 01:00:34.929
Tell me.

01:00:34.989 --> 01:00:35.900
Not...

01:00:35.960 --> 01:00:37.197
not one zero.

01:00:37.258 --> 01:00:38.415
No.

01:00:38.476 --> 01:00:40.638
It is not one zero.

01:00:40.698 --> 01:00:42.538
Then who?

01:00:42.598 --> 01:00:44.600
It is Cheggi.

01:00:44.660 --> 01:00:46.290
Cheggi!

01:00:46.350 --> 01:00:48.082
My son!

01:00:48.143 --> 01:00:49.724
Where?

01:00:49.784 --> 01:00:54.926
He is in the field of the M's outside the village.

01:00:54.986 --> 01:00:58.038
No!

01:00:58.098 --> 01:01:01.532
The lion has killed my son!

01:01:01.592 --> 01:01:06.110
Even if it is a white lion, I will kill it.

01:01:06.170 --> 01:01:09.846
I will kill it with my band!

01:01:09.906 --> 01:01:10.627
Ohhh!

01:01:10.687 --> 01:01:18.730
Check it!

01:01:18.790 --> 01:01:26.334
Where is she?

01:01:26.394 --> 01:01:28.535
Where is Jata?

01:01:28.595 --> 01:01:33.923
Inside.

01:01:33.983 --> 01:01:39.601
I'm here.

01:01:39.662 --> 01:01:40.912
Speak to me.

01:01:40.972 --> 01:01:42.513
Why, Chegg.

01:01:42.573 --> 01:01:44.364
He was so good.

01:01:44.424 --> 01:01:46.084
So fine.

01:01:46.144 --> 01:01:49.916
This holy lion ripped out my son's heart.

01:01:49.976 --> 01:01:52.218
I want to die.

01:01:52.278 --> 01:01:54.208
I want to die too.

01:01:54.268 --> 01:01:56.671
You know what they are saying.

01:01:56.731 --> 01:02:00.973
That it's punishing our tribe because of your actions.

01:02:01.033 --> 01:02:03.914
The child wakira saw it in the water.

01:02:03.974 --> 01:02:06.305
But I've done only good.

01:02:06.365 --> 01:02:08.845
I've brought water to our fields.

01:02:08.905 --> 01:02:12.556
Because of this, our crops grow well.

01:02:12.616 --> 01:02:16.558
Then maybe it's because you are dealing with white men.

01:02:16.618 --> 01:02:26.524
Whatever it is, it's too late for my son.

01:02:26.584 --> 01:02:32.730
Here they come.

01:02:32.770 --> 01:02:33.550
Wanjiro and Jata.

01:02:33.570 --> 01:02:34.120
Poor Jata.

01:02:34.180 --> 01:02:35.751
She looks ready to die.

01:02:35.771 --> 01:02:37.572
Poor Wanjiro, his oldest son.

01:02:37.612 --> 01:02:38.752
The meeting started.

01:02:38.772 --> 01:02:39.693
Let us begin.

01:02:39.713 --> 01:02:51.444
You have all heard the news.

01:02:51.504 --> 01:03:04.217
Wanjiro, Jata.

01:03:04.278 --> 01:03:06.939
Words cannot express our grief.

01:03:06.999 --> 01:03:10.062
We are grieving with you.

01:03:10.122 --> 01:03:12.853
Thank you, my friends.

01:03:12.914 --> 01:03:15.675
It's time to take action.

01:03:15.735 --> 01:03:17.866
What should we do, Wanjiro?

01:03:17.926 --> 01:03:20.838
Find this animal and kill it.

01:03:20.898 --> 01:03:23.590
Wanjiro, what is it, Jumbo?

01:03:23.650 --> 01:03:29.044
First, please accept my sorrow at the death of your son, Chegg.

01:03:29.104 --> 01:03:30.622
Thank you, Jumbo.

01:03:30.683 --> 01:03:32.962
but I have to repeat.

01:03:33.022 --> 01:03:37.138
The animal which killed your son is a white lion.

01:03:37.198 --> 01:03:43.937
The white lion is a spirit who has come to punish us because of our evil deeds.

01:03:43.997 --> 01:03:50.405
In fact, Because of your evil deeds, One Zero.

01:03:50.465 --> 01:03:57.040
I don't know what you think you are saying, but I will tell you, One Zero.

01:03:57.100 --> 01:04:02.183
The lion is punishing us because of your dealings with the white man.

01:04:02.243 --> 01:04:04.905
Please explain your meaning, Jumbo.

01:04:04.965 --> 01:04:06.946
Listen to my words, everyone.

01:04:07.006 --> 01:04:09.978
Chief One Zero wants to build a natural reserve.

01:04:10.038 --> 01:04:12.250
We all know this, Jumbo.

01:04:12.310 --> 01:04:14.741
But there is something you do not know.

01:04:14.801 --> 01:04:19.882
Chief Wanduro has made a secret arrangement with the white men.

01:04:19.942 --> 01:04:34.085
He plans to sell them land near the coast so that they can build an airport, roads, hotels, expensive places that only foreigners can afford.

01:04:34.145 --> 01:04:40.256
This is a secret plan, and the white men will pay one jello for this!

01:04:40.316 --> 01:04:41.507
What?!

01:04:41.567 --> 01:04:41.947
What?!

01:04:41.967 --> 01:04:43.258
What happened to you?!

01:04:43.318 --> 01:04:45.330
How of this nonsense, Jomo?!

01:04:45.370 --> 01:04:47.711
You met with these men last week?

01:04:47.771 --> 01:04:48.462
Yes!

01:04:48.522 --> 01:04:50.373
Everyone knows that!

01:04:50.433 --> 01:04:54.556
Someone else from our people was at that meeting.

01:04:54.616 --> 01:04:55.376
Yes!

01:04:55.437 --> 01:04:58.248
Morithi was with me when I met them.

01:04:58.308 --> 01:05:03.508
Morithi, tell the rest of us about the meeting.

01:05:03.568 --> 01:05:06.734
It is exactly as Chumbo said.

01:05:06.794 --> 01:05:11.028
You thought I would stay silent if the white men paid me enough.

01:05:11.088 --> 01:05:14.320
But you were wrong.

01:05:14.380 --> 01:05:17.842
What are you saying?

01:05:17.902 --> 01:05:21.304
It is time for you to go and you.

01:05:21.364 --> 01:05:24.276
You and Jata are in disgrace.

01:05:24.336 --> 01:05:29.492
You must leave the village.

01:05:29.553 --> 01:05:33.308
Hello?

01:05:33.368 --> 01:05:35.229
Jim, it's Mike.

01:05:35.289 --> 01:05:36.649
Hi, Mike.

01:05:36.709 --> 01:05:37.879
How's it going?

01:05:37.939 --> 01:05:40.630
Did you get to see Chief Wenjiro today?

01:05:40.690 --> 01:05:42.170
No, I didn't.

01:05:42.230 --> 01:05:46.501
Listen, Jim, something strange is going on down there.

01:05:46.561 --> 01:05:50.342
Wenjiro has been sent out of the village in disgrace.

01:05:50.402 --> 01:05:51.402
What?

01:05:51.462 --> 01:05:52.323
Why?

01:05:52.343 --> 01:05:54.523
I've been trying to find out.

01:05:54.583 --> 01:06:02.639
What I do know is that a guy called Morithi is the new chief, but the medicine man Chumbo?

01:06:02.699 --> 01:06:04.350
Yeah, that's him.

01:06:04.410 --> 01:06:09.661
He's the one who's really in charge, and he doesn't want to have anything to do with us.

01:06:09.722 --> 01:06:11.062
Oh, no.

01:06:11.122 --> 01:06:13.002
This is terrible.

01:06:13.062 --> 01:06:15.263
All that work wasted.

01:06:15.323 --> 01:06:17.134
Where is Wenjiro?

01:06:17.194 --> 01:06:20.878
He and his wife have moved into an apartment here in Malindi.

01:06:20.938 --> 01:06:23.012
an apartment in the town?

01:06:23.072 --> 01:06:25.424
For a village tribal chief?

01:06:25.484 --> 01:06:26.324
Yes.

01:06:26.384 --> 01:06:28.206
But there's something else.

01:06:28.266 --> 01:06:33.141
I was in the main street of Melindy this morning, and I saw Chumbo.

01:06:33.201 --> 01:06:35.753
You saw Chumbo in town?

01:06:35.813 --> 01:06:36.764
Yes.

01:06:36.824 --> 01:06:46.700
I've seen him here a few times, but this morning I saw him talking to a couple of South African guys, Tim Hawkins and Monty Klein.

01:06:46.761 --> 01:06:48.219
I don't know them.

01:06:48.279 --> 01:06:48.909
Do you?

01:06:48.970 --> 01:06:50.270
Not personally.

01:06:50.330 --> 01:06:51.102
No.

01:06:51.162 --> 01:06:53.273
But I know who they are.

01:06:53.333 --> 01:06:57.376
They've both been in prison for illegal ivory trading.

01:06:57.436 --> 01:06:59.188
My God.

01:06:59.248 --> 01:07:01.169
What do you think we should do?

01:07:01.229 --> 01:07:05.212
Well, first of all, we should go and see Wangiru.

01:07:05.272 --> 01:07:06.363
I agree.

01:07:06.423 --> 01:07:18.746
I'll come and pick you up.

01:07:18.806 --> 01:07:30.739
Hello, Jada.

01:07:30.799 --> 01:07:34.830
Bruno, hello, come in.

01:07:34.890 --> 01:07:37.231
Is Juan Julu here?

01:07:37.291 --> 01:07:40.702
Yes, follow me.

01:07:40.762 --> 01:07:43.523
Juan Julu.

01:07:43.583 --> 01:07:47.184
Bruno, this is an unexpected pleasure.

01:07:47.244 --> 01:07:48.914
Come in and sit down.

01:07:48.974 --> 01:07:50.525
I will bring some water.

01:07:50.585 --> 01:07:53.036
Thank you.

01:07:53.096 --> 01:07:58.404
This must be very difficult for you, Chief, to live here, like this.

01:07:58.464 --> 01:08:00.161
We're all right.

01:08:00.221 --> 01:08:02.032
Tell me your news.

01:08:02.092 --> 01:08:04.684
Moritha has been elected chief.

01:08:04.744 --> 01:08:06.086
Moritha?

01:08:06.146 --> 01:08:07.166
Hmm.

01:08:07.226 --> 01:08:08.818
Interesting.

01:08:08.878 --> 01:08:12.400
But Chumbo is the one with the power, no doubt.

01:08:12.460 --> 01:08:16.152
Bruno, I have to ask you something.

01:08:16.213 --> 01:08:22.228
Did you believe Moritha's story that I secretly agreed to sell land to the white men?

01:08:22.287 --> 01:08:27.266
Do you believe that I would do that after all the years you've known me?

01:08:27.326 --> 01:08:28.842
Do you believe me?

01:08:28.902 --> 01:08:31.613
Or do you believe Morithi?

01:08:31.674 --> 01:08:33.444
No, Chief.

01:08:33.504 --> 01:08:34.965
But why would he...

01:08:34.985 --> 01:08:37.206
You can't see why he would lie.

01:08:37.266 --> 01:08:38.077
No.

01:08:38.137 --> 01:08:40.399
Neither can I.

01:08:40.458 --> 01:08:42.250
Goodness.

01:08:42.310 --> 01:08:44.960
So many visitors today.

01:08:45.020 --> 01:08:47.762
I will get to see the chief.

01:08:47.822 --> 01:08:48.803
Oh, I'll take this look.

01:08:48.863 --> 01:08:49.724
Follow me, please.

01:08:49.783 --> 01:08:50.584
Of course.

01:08:50.644 --> 01:08:52.685
Thank you.

01:08:52.745 --> 01:08:53.176
One zero.

01:08:53.236 --> 01:08:56.274
The men from the aid development are here.

01:08:56.333 --> 01:09:00.161
Mike, hello, so good to see you.

01:09:00.221 --> 01:09:01.842
Hello, Wangeiro.

01:09:01.902 --> 01:09:05.002
This is Runo, one of my oldest friends.

01:09:05.062 --> 01:09:06.403
Please to meet you, Runo.

01:09:06.463 --> 01:09:08.573
This is my colleague, Jim Ray.

01:09:08.633 --> 01:09:09.864
Hi.

01:09:09.924 --> 01:09:14.365
Wangeiro, I have something important to tell you.

01:09:14.425 --> 01:09:16.896
Can we speak privately for a moment?

01:09:16.956 --> 01:09:21.368
Mike, anything you want to say, you can say in front of Runo.

01:09:21.428 --> 01:09:24.971
Okay, I have some news for you.

01:09:25.032 --> 01:09:28.524
I saw Chimbo this morning, here in Melindy.

01:09:28.584 --> 01:09:29.375
Really?

01:09:29.435 --> 01:09:30.796
What was he doing?

01:09:30.856 --> 01:09:33.728
He was talking to a couple of South Africans.

01:09:33.788 --> 01:09:39.713
They're criminals, lawbreakers, a couple of poachers who are well known to the police.

01:09:39.772 --> 01:09:43.616
They make their money selling elephant tusks on the black market.

01:09:43.676 --> 01:09:45.437
This is unbelievable.

01:09:45.497 --> 01:09:46.958
Of course.

01:09:47.018 --> 01:09:49.409
Now it all makes sense.

01:09:49.468 --> 01:09:53.598
This is why Chumbo was against the Nature Reserve.

01:09:53.658 --> 01:10:01.090
If we have a Nature Reserve, the land will be patrolled by wardens and poachers will have a difficult time.

01:10:01.150 --> 01:10:03.751
We have no proof of this, of course.

01:10:03.811 --> 01:10:05.521
No, that's right.

01:10:05.581 --> 01:10:08.052
But this is gonna affect us too.

01:10:08.112 --> 01:10:11.873
So we're planning to keep an eye on Chumbo for the next few days.

01:10:11.933 --> 01:10:13.944
Yes, please do that.

01:10:14.004 --> 01:10:15.574
I will help you.

01:10:15.634 --> 01:10:16.954
Thank you, Bruno.

01:10:17.014 --> 01:10:22.134
It is the least I can do for an old friend.

01:10:22.194 --> 01:10:27.104
It's good of you to help us, Bruno.

01:10:27.164 --> 01:10:30.336
We've invested a lot of money in this project.

01:10:30.396 --> 01:10:35.108
If the people in the village tell us to leave, it will all be wasted.

01:10:35.168 --> 01:10:37.589
Most people are thankful for the work you have done.

01:10:37.609 --> 01:10:39.960
I'm glad to hear it.

01:10:40.020 --> 01:10:41.181
Okay.

01:10:41.241 --> 01:10:44.523
You want us to drop you away from the village, right?

01:10:44.583 --> 01:10:45.243
Yes.

01:10:45.303 --> 01:10:48.254
I prefer to work the last few miles by myself.

01:10:48.314 --> 01:10:49.635
Okay.

01:10:49.695 --> 01:10:51.896
Where are you going, Mike?

01:10:51.936 --> 01:10:53.824
You took a wrong turning there.

01:10:53.884 --> 01:10:55.102
Did I?

01:10:55.162 --> 01:10:57.514
Is this the wrong way, Bruno?

01:10:57.574 --> 01:11:02.218
Well, it is also possible to get to the village down this road.

01:11:02.278 --> 01:11:04.890
So, what's down here?

01:11:04.950 --> 01:11:09.404
It leads to the Nakuru Cave, a very sacred place.

01:11:09.464 --> 01:11:14.108
No one except the chief and the medicine man are allowed to visit it.

01:11:14.168 --> 01:11:17.120
I see.

01:11:17.180 --> 01:11:21.414
Boy, this is a rough road.

01:11:21.474 --> 01:11:23.910
What's that light up ahead?

01:11:23.970 --> 01:11:27.936
But, that is where the cave is.

01:11:27.996 --> 01:11:30.527
But there should be no light there.

01:11:30.587 --> 01:11:37.048
Maybe we should take a look.

01:11:37.108 --> 01:11:45.720
Let's go and see what's going on.

01:11:45.780 --> 01:11:51.242
We are here, the Nakuruke.

01:11:51.302 --> 01:11:54.189
Well, there's no one here now.

01:11:54.249 --> 01:11:57.627
But there was someone here a while ago.

01:11:57.687 --> 01:11:59.508
There's a fire burning.

01:11:59.568 --> 01:12:01.410
Let's take a look around.

01:12:01.470 --> 01:12:02.681
Look at this!

01:12:02.741 --> 01:12:03.832
What is it?

01:12:03.892 --> 01:12:05.944
It's a lion's head mask.

01:12:06.004 --> 01:12:10.066
And this thing next to it looks like an old rug.

01:12:10.126 --> 01:12:11.397
Phew!

01:12:11.437 --> 01:12:12.758
What a smell!

01:12:12.818 --> 01:12:15.530
This is the coat of a lion.

01:12:15.590 --> 01:12:17.442
Are you sure?

01:12:17.502 --> 01:12:19.874
Lion coats aren't this color.

01:12:19.934 --> 01:12:23.159
This is creamy white.

01:12:23.219 --> 01:12:25.673
Of course!

01:12:25.733 --> 01:12:27.304
The white lion!

01:12:27.364 --> 01:12:28.864
And look at this!

01:12:28.924 --> 01:12:33.896
A huge tape recorder!

01:12:33.956 --> 01:12:37.818
Jesus!

01:12:37.878 --> 01:12:39.288
Did you hear that?

01:12:39.348 --> 01:12:41.469
A white lion's coat?

01:12:41.529 --> 01:12:44.910
And a tape recording of a roaring lion?

01:12:44.970 --> 01:12:49.752
I think we should take these things and show them to the people in the village.

01:12:49.812 --> 01:12:53.158
Come on!

01:12:53.218 --> 01:13:04.122
People, people welcome to my first meeting as your new chief.

01:13:04.142 --> 01:13:07.785
I want to tell you my plans for the future of the village.

01:13:07.825 --> 01:13:08.666
What is that noise?

01:13:08.686 --> 01:13:09.366
Who is there?

01:13:09.386 --> 01:13:16.262
The white men are here in the Land Rover.

01:13:16.322 --> 01:13:23.546
The white men, how dare they!

01:13:23.606 --> 01:13:25.166
And Runo is with them!

01:13:25.226 --> 01:13:29.218
We are coming here to the meeting!

01:13:29.278 --> 01:13:30.648
Don't let them in!

01:13:30.708 --> 01:13:31.729
Chumbo!

01:13:31.789 --> 01:13:35.340
Please don't say that we must let them in!

01:13:35.400 --> 01:13:38.391
Should I open the door and let them in?

01:13:38.451 --> 01:13:42.202
Yes, yes, let them in!

01:13:42.262 --> 01:13:48.394
Greetings, Chief Morithi and Medicine Man Chumbo!

01:13:48.454 --> 01:13:50.175
What do you want?

01:13:50.235 --> 01:13:53.516
We have come to pay our respects to the new chief.

01:13:53.576 --> 01:13:58.039
Well, you can do this, and then you can leave.

01:13:58.099 --> 01:14:00.080
Okay, we'll do that.

01:14:00.140 --> 01:14:06.216
But first, we want to show you some things that we found at the Nakuro Cave.

01:14:06.276 --> 01:14:09.718
You have been to the Nakuro Cave?

01:14:09.778 --> 01:14:11.750
Yes, we have.

01:14:11.810 --> 01:14:14.712
Bruno, you had no right to go there.

01:14:14.772 --> 01:14:18.606
The Nakuro Cave is a sacred place for our people.

01:14:18.666 --> 01:14:21.408
If you took them there, you will be punished.

01:14:21.468 --> 01:14:28.360
Well, before you decide on Bruno's punishment, take a look at this lion's head mask.

01:14:28.420 --> 01:14:33.392
And this lion's coat, which has been painted white.

01:14:33.452 --> 01:14:36.353
And we also found this tape recorder.

01:14:36.413 --> 01:14:43.026
Let's listen to the tape, shall we?

01:14:43.086 --> 01:14:53.331
So, you see, the white men were responsible for the white lion.

01:14:53.391 --> 01:14:54.992
They tried to trick us.

01:14:55.052 --> 01:14:56.604
No, Chumbo.

01:14:56.664 --> 01:14:59.716
You and Marithi are the guilty ones.

01:14:59.776 --> 01:15:06.728
You and your South African friends who have been killing elephants and stealing their tusks for ivory.

01:15:06.788 --> 01:15:13.731
You are the ones who killed Chege and sent Wenjiro into exile for crimes he did not commit.

01:15:13.751 --> 01:15:14.071
It was Jumbo.

01:15:14.091 --> 01:15:14.421
